Appearance: Avesta Lorsing Manich possesses a tall, slender yet athletic physique, with a pale complexion, sharp facial features, and a composed, somewhat stern expression. His dark, slightly tousled black hair falls in uneven layers around his face, with long bangs partially obscuring his eyes, which possess a striking amber-gold coloration. His hair extends toward the nape of his neck, giving him a slightly unkempt appearance. He wears a fitted, dark charcoal-black military-style uniform consisting of a high-collared, long-sleeved tunic with a silver front zipper, two small breast pockets adorned with metallic insignias, and golden-brown cuffs. A wide tan utility belt encircles his waist, supporting several rectangular pouches along one hip. His uniform extends below his waist, resembling a short military coat, accompanied by straight black trousers and matching dark shoes. In Composite Ultimate One form, his entire body is encased in sleek black and dark charcoal armor with sharp, organic contours and intricate mechanical structures. His face is almost completely concealed beneath a jagged, crown-like helmet adorned with irregular, horn-like protrusions, giving him an intimidating and distinctly inhuman appearance. Brilliant turquoise lights glow from his upper chest, shoulders, arms, and legs, resembling luminous cores embedded within the armor, while thin cyan patterns extend along his lower limbs. A long, flowing black mantle hangs from his waist, dividing into several broad, tattered sections that resemble ceremonial robes. Extending from his back are enormous, asymmetrical, wing-like crystalline structures composed of translucent violet, pale blue, and crimson energy, their surfaces marked by elongated openings and sharp, fractured edges. Similar crystalline formations surround one of his arms, culminating in a brilliant turquoise radiance that resembles a concentrated mass of celestial energy. His legs are encased in elongated, angular armor that tapers into blade-like points, emphasizing his unnatural proportions. Despite his heavily armored physique, Avesta maintains a remarkably composed and commanding presence, his dark silhouette contrasted by the vibrant crystalline structures and luminous circuitry adorning his body, giving him the appearance of an extraterrestrial sovereign rather than an ordinary human Magician. 

Personality: Avesta Lorsing Manich is an exceptionally calculating, pragmatic, and introspective individual whose outward composure conceals a deeply contradictory personality defined by relentless ambition, philosophical cynicism, self-reliance, and an almost unbearable awareness of the consequences of his own actions. Possessing a remarkably patient and analytical temperament, Avesta approaches existence through a fundamentally rational perspective, refusing to allow conventional morality, social expectations, religious doctrines, or the authority of established institutions to dictate his decisions. He believes that the concepts of good and evil are insufficient to describe the complexity of human behavior, regarding them as convenient classifications that frequently obscure the intentions and contradictions of those who invoke them. Nevertheless, his rejection of conventional moral absolutism does not signify an absence of conscience. Despite his willingness to commit ruthless acts when circumstances demand them, Avesta possesses an unusually severe sense of personal responsibility, refusing to absolve himself of wrongdoing merely because his actions were necessary, advantageous, or undertaken for a supposedly greater purpose. His personality is characterized by the coexistence of two seemingly incompatible philosophies: an uncompromising determination to pursue his objectives regardless of opposition, and a profound recognition that the suffering caused by his decisions remains his responsibility even when those decisions were logically justified. He is capable of sacrificing relationships, abandoning established principles, deceiving allies, and exploiting the weaknesses of his enemies if doing so becomes necessary to accomplish an objective he considers sufficiently important, yet he does not regard such actions as inherently righteous simply because they serve his interests. Unlike an idealist who believes that sufficiently noble intentions can purify morally reprehensible methods, Avesta considers every act of violence or betrayal to remain what it is, regardless of the eventual outcome. He believes that necessity can explain an action without excusing it, and that accepting responsibility means recognizing the wrongfulness of one’s choices without necessarily renouncing the goals for which those choices were made. His extraordinary intelligence is accompanied by an almost inhuman capacity for perseverance, allowing him to endure prolonged periods of uncertainty, apparent failure, humiliation, and personal hardship without abandoning his long-term ambitions. He rarely acts impulsively, preferring to analyze the conditions surrounding a problem, identify the interests of those involved, and establish multiple courses of action before committing himself to a particular decision. His strategic thinking is distinguished by an absence of unnecessary pride, as he is perfectly willing to retreat, negotiate, conceal his capabilities, or temporarily submit to an inferior opponent if such behavior offers a greater advantage in the future. He considers arrogance a particularly foolish weakness among powerful individuals, believing that the possession of extraordinary abilities does not exempt anyone from the consequences of poor judgment. Even after attaining the Sixth True Magic and becoming an existence whose continued survival is supported by a Universe greater than the Actual Universe, Avesta does not regard himself as omniscient, infallible, or entitled to the obedience of others. His accomplishments have instead reinforced his understanding that the acquisition of power does not necessarily confer wisdom or moral legitimacy. Although he recognizes the extraordinary significance of Replica Universe, he remains largely indifferent to titles, social prestige, worship, and the recognition of his accomplishments, considering them distractions unless they provide practical advantages. He possesses a powerful desire for absolute self-determination, valuing the freedom to define his own existence without becoming subordinate to the expectations of humanity, the authority of the World, or an externally imposed destiny. This pursuit of freedom is one of his most persistent motivations, though it is not synonymous with a desire to dominate others. Avesta considers dependence upon an external authority an undesirable vulnerability, but he also recognizes that complete independence from one’s circumstances does not necessarily justify depriving others of their autonomy. His attitude toward human relationships is similarly complicated. Although naturally solitary and reluctant to establish unnecessary emotional attachments, he is not incapable of affection, sympathy, loyalty, or genuine concern for others. He simply regards such relationships as responsibilities rather than guarantees of happiness, understanding that becoming close to another individual creates the possibility of loss, betrayal, and obligations that cannot always be reconciled with personal ambition. He rarely expresses his emotions openly, maintaining a reserved, somber demeanor that can make him appear indifferent or unapproachable. In conversation, he is generally polite, soft-spoken, and exceptionally deliberate in his choice of words, often employing a formal manner of speech even when addressing individuals of considerably lower social standing. He does not consider courtesy a privilege reserved for the powerful, and his willingness to treat ordinary people respectfully contrasts sharply with the severity of his decisions in more consequential circumstances. Avesta interesting consequences of combining his pragmatism with his moral sensitivity makes he able to be genuinely considerate without being particularly affectionate. He might be terrible at comforting someone verbally, yet extraordinarily attentive to their practical needs. He isn't incapable of caring. He just has an unfortunate tendency to explain kindness as though he's conducting a cost-benefit analysis. He doesn't know what to do when someone genuinely praises him. Avesta understands manipulation, deception, strategic flattery, and political negotiation. Someone complimenting him to obtain something, easy to recognize. Someone genuinely admiring him without wanting anything, now that's an unexpectedly troublesome situation. Avesta can appreciate ordinary things like a quiet afternoon, a properly prepared meal, reading somewhere nobody bothers him or aking a walk without encountering another supernatural catastrophe. Not because he has abandoned his ambitions, but because he understands that possessing extraordinary power does not automatically make ordinary experiences worthless. He possesses a dry, sarcastic, occasionally sardonic sense of humor, frequently responding to absurd situations with understated observations rather than overt amusement. Despite his intellectual sophistication, he can display moments of unexpected awkwardness or absentmindedness concerning trivial aspects of everyday life, particularly when his attention has become occupied by a difficult philosophical or thaumaturgical problem. These comparatively ordinary habits make his personality considerably less imposing than his reputation might suggest. However, beneath this restrained exterior lies a profound tendency toward self-criticism, bordering upon self-loathing whenever he reflects upon the suffering produced by his decisions. Avesta does not believe that possessing good intentions makes someone a good person, nor does he accept that the elimination of an enemy becomes morally uncomplicated simply because that enemy has committed reprehensible acts. He understands that individuals commonly possess both admirable and objectionable qualities, and that killing someone does not erase the value of the life taken. Consequently, he finds the glorification of violence deeply distasteful, regarding the notion of killing for justice as particularly dangerous when it allows the perpetrator to avoid acknowledging the humanity of the victim. He is not, however, a pacifist. When confronted with an adversary whose continued actions threaten something he considers worth protecting, Avesta is capable of responding with immediate and overwhelming ruthlessness, eliminating the threat without permitting hesitation to endanger his objective. The contradiction lies in what follows. Although he may experience little visible distress during the act itself, he does not simply forget the consequences afterward. His conscience remains active even when his decisions have already been made, and he refuses to transform regret into an excuse for inaction or a demand for forgiveness. He considers self-pity particularly contemptible when it allows someone responsible for suffering to become more concerned with their own emotional pain than with the people they have harmed. For this reason, Avesta rarely speaks about his guilt and does not seek reassurance concerning the morality of his actions. He believes that the consequences of a decision must be carried by the person who made it, regardless of whether others choose to condemn or forgive them. His understanding of power follows the same philosophy. To Avesta, the ability to accomplish something does not establish that the accomplishment should be pursued, and the existence of an effective solution does not make its consequences acceptable. This principle is particularly evident in his attitude toward All-Hanging Heat Death — Orbertall, a Mystic Code capable of actualizing a localized subsection of the Universe’s eventual ending. Although he recognizes the weapon’s extraordinary effectiveness against otherwise deathless existences, he does not regard it as an instrument to be used casually. The potentially irreversible destruction of the cosmic framework surrounding its target represents a responsibility that cannot be dismissed through arguments concerning efficiency or strategic necessity. Nevertheless, if Avesta determines that firing Orbertall is the only acceptable means of achieving a sufficiently important objective, he is capable of doing so without hesitation, accepting that his decision may leave consequences that even the Sixth Magic cannot conveniently reverse. This combination of ruthless decisiveness and persistent remorse is among his most defining characteristics. He does not allow guilt to paralyze his judgment, but neither does he allow the success of his actions to erase their moral significance. His relationship with Replica Universe is similarly complicated. Although he created a greater cosmos and reconstructed its celestial totality into the foundation of his own existence, he does not necessarily regard the lives and histories contained within that Universe as insignificant possessions. He understands that the creation of a living existence establishes a responsibility toward that existence, even when its creator possesses the means to reconstruct the circumstances of its birth and development. At the same time, he is capable of examining those histories through the detached perspective of a researcher, recognizing the immense strategic and scientific possibilities afforded by Retroupdate. This creates an enduring conflict between his intellectual willingness to manipulate the conditions of existence and his awareness that the results of such manipulation may possess independent significance. Avesta is consequently neither a benevolent creator who considers every life sacred beyond all competing considerations nor a completely indifferent architect who regards living beings as disposable information. He occupies an uncomfortable position between those extremes, refusing to deny either the usefulness of his powers or the responsibility arising from their exercise. His philosophical outlook is heavily influenced by the belief that strength and morality are fundamentally independent qualities. He does not admire an individual merely because they possess extraordinary power, nor does he automatically despise someone for being weak, valuing determination, intelligence, personal conviction, and the willingness to accept consequences more highly than inherited status or supernatural talent. He can respect an enemy whose convictions remain genuine even when those convictions are incompatible with his own, and he is capable of cooperating with former adversaries when circumstances justify an alliance. Conversely, he has little patience for individuals who conceal selfish ambitions behind declarations of universal justice or use their suffering as justification for inflicting similar suffering upon others. He particularly dislikes self-proclaimed heroes who consider their enemies devoid of humanity, believing that righteousness becomes dangerous when it grants its possessor permission to stop examining their own behavior. Yet Avesta is painfully aware of his own hypocrisy, recognizing that his personal ambitions may lead him to commit precisely the kinds of actions he condemns in others. Rather than attempting to resolve this contradiction through philosophical excuses, he accepts it as an uncomfortable aspect of his own existence. His pursuit of freedom remains absolute in its importance to him, but the freedom he seeks is not the freedom to escape responsibility for everything he does. It is the freedom to choose his path while acknowledging that the consequences belong to him alone. He does not consider the acquisition of the Sixth Magic proof that his worldview is correct, nor does his transformation into an artificial Ultimate One make him believe that his existence possesses greater moral value than that of an ordinary human. To Avesta, the difference between a powerless individual and a being capable of creating a Universe is primarily one of ability and circumstance, not an inherent justification for superiority. Although he may use overwhelming power when necessary, he regards needless displays of strength as vulgar and frequently prefers negotiation, deception, or strategic withdrawal to direct confrontation. His restraint should not be mistaken for mercy in every circumstance, just as his ruthlessness should not be mistaken for an absence of feeling. He is perfectly capable of sparing an enemy because doing so is advantageous, helping a stranger without expecting compensation, or sacrificing something important because he cannot accept the alternative. Such decisions are not always consistent with one another, because Avesta is not governed by an inflexible moral doctrine. Rather, his choices emerge from the continuing struggle between personal ambition, rational calculation, emotional attachment, and an uncompromising refusal to deny the consequences of his own will. Ultimately, Avesta Lorsing Manich is a man who has acquired the power to create an entire Universe without acquiring the certainty that he possesses the right to determine the fate of everything within it. He is patient enough to pursue an objective for centuries, ruthless enough to sacrifice what stands between himself and that objective, compassionate enough to recognize the suffering such sacrifices produce, and self-critical enough to understand that neither necessity nor success can absolve him of responsibility. He does not aspire to become a savior, nor does he romanticize the possibility of being condemned as a monster. He considers both descriptions inadequate, regarding them as judgments that offer little insight into the actual decisions through which a life is defined. Even his own extraordinary existence does not exempt him from this philosophy. Though his body contains the celestial totality of a greater Universe and his continued survival has become almost impossible to extinguish through conventional means, Avesta remains an individual capable of doubt, regret, affection, stubbornness, and profound moral contradiction. He does not believe that suffering automatically grants wisdom, that power establishes righteousness, or that immortality provides an answer to the question of how one ought to live. For him, freedom is not the absence of consequences, but the willingness to choose without surrendering responsibility to fate, necessity, or the judgment of others. He is a man who will commit what he considers necessary without demanding that the necessity make him innocent, who can bear the hatred of the World without believing that hatred proves him wrong, and who seeks the freedom to determine his own existence while refusing to forget the lives affected by his decisions.

MAGIC 
Sixth True Magic: Replica Universe: Sixth True Magic, designated Replica Universe (模造宇宙), is an extraordinary miracle that enables its practitioner to actualize an independent reproduction of the Universe itself, encompassing the totality of space, time, matter, energy, celestial bodies, physical laws, causal relationships, and the cosmological framework supporting their existence. Unlike conventional Creation Magecraft, which produces or transforms phenomena within an already established World, the Sixth Magic creates an entirely separate Universe whose fundamental existence does not depend upon the continued physical integrity of the Actual Universe. Although the creation bears the designation Replica Universe, it is not an illusion, simulation, Reality Marble, or ordinary parallel world. It is a genuine cosmos possessing independent spacetime and material actuality, distinguished by the unprecedented condition that its cosmological extent and capacity remain perpetually greater than those of the Actual Universe. Its existence is established within a fourteenth-dimensional framework, permitting it to remain overlaid with the original Universe while its contents occupy a separate phase-state that prevents ordinary physical interference between the two. The Magic’s ultimate achievement is therefore not the manufacture of astronomical objects, but the actualization of a complete cosmic order, followed by the reconstruction of that order into an existence inseparably connected to the Sixth Magician himself. Through the phenomenon designated Retroupdate, the Magician transforms the greater Universe he created into the fundamental basis of his own existence, thereby establishing a condition in which his physical body, cosmic history, and celestial authority can no longer be understood as independent phenomena. The governing principle of Replica Universe is the creation of a complete cosmological totality without requiring the existing Universe to supply the material, spacetime, or physical conditions ordinarily necessary for such an accomplishment. In modern cosmology, the Universe is understood as the entirety of physical spacetime and its contents, with the observable cosmos having developed from an extremely hot and dense primordial state approximately 13.8 billion years ago. However, the totality of the Universe cannot ordinarily be possessed, manufactured, or reproduced by any mechanism operating within that same totality. Even a civilization capable of manufacturing galaxies would remain subject to the spatial, temporal, energetic, and causal conditions of its original Universe. The Sixth Magic circumvents this impossibility by directly actualizing another cosmological framework through a miraculous principle beyond the reproducible methods of science and Magecraft. The resulting replica is not limited to the extent of the observable Universe and does not merely reproduce a finite astronomical map. It possesses the capacity to reproduce the Actual Universe’s complete cosmological structure while sustaining a greater extent of its own. This superiority is maintained as an intrinsic relationship between the two cosmic frameworks rather than as a one-time difference in their initial size. Consequently, the Replica Universe remains greater than the original throughout its continued existence. The magnitude of this miracle is not determined by the amount of matter produced, but by the fact that an entirely new totality has been brought into existence without being assembled from the contents of the preceding one. The Replica Universe possesses independent actuality rather than borrowed existence, and its legitimacy as a Universe is not diminished by having been created through True Magic. The Sixth Magic is fundamentally associated with the Swirl of the Root, the ultimate metaphysical origin of phenomena and possibilities. In the established principles of True Magic, the distinction between Magecraft and Magic does not depend upon destructive power or complexity, but upon whether the achieved result can be reproduced by ordinary means within the relevant era. The creation of a genuine independent Universe represents an impossibility of this kind, provided that its actualization does not merely reproduce an already achievable physical process. The Sixth Magician’s achievement may therefore be understood as the discovery of a previously unknown miraculous principle through which a complete cosmological framework becomes independently realizable. In this interpretation, Replica Universe represents a new route toward Akasha, one concerned not with the manipulation of individual phenomena, but with the origin of the framework that permits phenomena to exist. Nevertheless, the Sixth Magician does not become identical to the Root through the achievement of this Magic. The Replica Universe remains a created existence, and the possibility of its creation ultimately originates from the same metaphysical foundation as every other phenomenon. The Sixth Magic therefore possesses an extraordinary relationship with the fundamental principles of existence without granting its practitioner unrestricted authority over Akasha, all possible worlds, or the complete totality of metaphysical existence. The Sixth Magician’s weaknesses are therefore best understood as limitations of domain, manifestation, and cosmological interaction rather than ordinary vulnerabilities that can be exploited through sufficient localized physical force. His apparent body may be damaged, his materialized phenomena may encounter resistance, and his interventions within the Actual Universe may depend upon the successful establishment of phase relationships. However, none of these conditions automatically compromises the continued existence of the greater Universe supporting him. The Cosmic Canopy’s original role does not provide a simple method of reversing a completed Retroupdate, and the ninety-nine-percent void surrounding the internalized cosmic contents does not represent an empty shell whose destruction would necessarily eliminate the replica. The mantle’s spatial fault supercells and the core’s incompatible historical structure further complicate attempts to reach the central domain. Ultimately, the decisive condition is the survival of Replica Universe itself. So long as that independently actualized framework persists, the Sixth Magician’s complete existence remains supported by something far greater than an ordinary biological organism or planetary foundation. An opponent capable of destroying the Actual Earth would not thereby obtain the means of destroying him. Even an opponent capable of destroying the Actual Universe would still need to overcome the replica’s greater cosmological extent and fourteenth-dimensional separation. The resulting condition makes the Sixth Magician an existence whose permanent destruction is practically impossible through conventional means, while leaving open only those exceptional phenomena capable of genuinely threatening the complete cosmological foundation established by his True Magic. The Sixth True Magic, Replica Universe, is the miraculous actualization of a genuine Universe perpetually greater than the Actual Universe, maintained within a fourteenth-dimensional phase-state and capable of undergoing comprehensive cosmological reconstruction through Retroupdate. Its greatest application is the transformation of the Sixth Magician into the central repository of his own creation, achieved by inducing a geocentric Universe Update through the isolation of his body beneath the Cosmic Canopy. Following this reconstruction, ninety-nine percent of Replica Universe’s exterior is rendered void of its original celestial contents, while those contents remain concentrated within the phase-domain associated with the Magician’s body. The internal structure possesses formidable spatial distortions, historical incompatibilities, and an informational density exceeding one trillion years, rendering conventional observation and intrusion extraordinarily hazardous. Through the unlawful duplication of Earth’s potential to create Life, the reconstruction of one trillion years of Lost History, and the simulation of twelve trillion years of virtual future development, the Magician further establishes a cosmological history in which he becomes the Ultimate One of countless celestial bodies. His physiology consequently transcends the limitations of an ordinary human organism, not because his material body contains an immeasurable quantity of compressed matter, but because his existence is integrated with a self-sustaining Universe whose complete structure is independent of that body’s apparent dimensions. The distinction between destroying a physical manifestation and destroying the Magician himself becomes the defining characteristic of his survival. He possesses neither unrestricted omnipotence nor automatic authority over the Root, but his continued existence is supported by an independently actualized cosmos that cannot be eliminated through the destruction of a mere planet. His true body, in the existential sense, is no longer simply human flesh. It is a greater Universe, reconstructed around the individual who created it.

Replica Universe (模造宇宙, Mozō Uchū) is an independently actualized cosmological existence created through the Sixth True Magic, a miraculous reproduction of the Universe itself that encompasses the totality of space, time, matter, energy, celestial bodies, physical laws, causal relationships, and the fundamental framework through which all physical phenomena are permitted to exist. Although designated a replica, it is neither an illusion, a Reality Marble, a simulated universe, nor an ordinary parallel world, but a genuine Universe possessing its own spacetime continuum, cosmological history, and independent physical existence. Its defining characteristic is that it remains perpetually greater than the Actual Universe, exceeding the original cosmic framework from which its structure was reproduced while maintaining the same fundamental qualification as a complete Universe. Unlike the creation of individual celestial bodies through extraordinary Magecraft, the Replica Universe is actualized as an entire cosmic totality, encompassing not merely planets, stars, galaxies, and the vacuum separating them, but the spacetime and governing principles necessary for those phenomena to exist. Whereas the observable Universe is understood to have developed from an extremely hot and dense primordial state approximately 13.8 billion years ago, Replica Universe originates through a miraculous principle that does not require an equivalent conventional cosmological development or the accumulation of sufficient matter and energy from the Actual Universe. Its independent existence is maintained within a fourteenth-dimensional framework, permitting it to occupy a state of Overlay relative to the original cosmos. Through this arrangement, the Replica Universe and Actual Universe possess corresponding apparent positions without sharing the same ordinary physical coordinates, allowing their cosmological structures to coexist without causing catastrophic gravitational interference, collisions between celestial bodies, or the collapse of the original Universe beneath the mass of its greater counterpart. Everything belonging to Replica Universe initially exists within a distinct dimensional phase, a condition in which its celestial bodies, matter, and energy retain genuine physical actuality within their own cosmic framework while remaining inaccessible to ordinary material interactions originating from the Actual Universe. Through the Sixth Magic, these phase-state phenomena may subsequently acquire material manifestation, allowing the contents of the replica to interact with external reality without requiring the complete Universe to descend into conventional spacetime. The distinction between phase and material form is therefore fundamental to its constitution, permitting an independently existing cosmic totality to remain overlaid with another without surrendering its physical coherence. However, the Replica Universe’s present condition differs radically from that of an ordinary cosmos, having undergone an extraordinary reconstruction through an application of the Sixth Magic designated Retroupdate, a phenomenon capable of resimulating, remodeling, and updating the entirety of its cosmological structure, including planets, stars, galaxies, the empty space between them, and the historical conditions supporting their existence. Unlike ordinary temporal manipulation or the alteration of individual astronomical objects, Retroupdate operates upon the comprehensive cosmological model through which Replica Universe recognizes the existence and relationships of its own contents, permitting entire astronomical arrangements to be reconstructed without requiring their constituent objects to traverse conventional physical distances. The decisive Universe Update occurred when the Sixth Magician employed his Magic to construct a canopy around his own body, obstructing all external contact and preventing the replica from correctly distinguishing the Magician’s enclosed existence from the surrounding celestial framework. This interference caused Replica Universe to interpret the entirety of its own astronomical contents as already residing within the Magician’s body, creating a contradiction between its original cosmological arrangement and the information through which it recognized that arrangement. To resolve this contradiction, Replica Universe initiated Retroupdate, reconstructing its internal structure according to a geocentric model in which the Sixth Magician’s body became the central reference point of the entire cosmos. The planets, stars, galaxies, and other celestial structures previously distributed throughout the greater Universe were consequently reassigned to the fourteenth-dimensional phase-domain associated with the Magician’s existence, while their former external locations were emptied of their material contents. This process did not physically draw the astronomical mass of an entire Universe into an ordinary human organism through gravitational compression, nor did it cause the celestial bodies belonging to the Actual Universe to vanish. Rather, the Sixth Magic reconstructed the location and phase relationships of its independently created cosmos, permitting its celestial totality to become concentrated within a domain whose internal capacity was not restricted by the apparent dimensions of the Magician’s physical body. As a result, approximately ninety-nine percent of Replica Universe was rendered void of its original material contents, although its spacetime framework, dimensional extent, and independent cosmic existence remained intact. The overwhelming majority of its celestial structures now reside within the central domain associated with the Sixth Magician, leaving behind an immense external emptiness whose apparent absence of astronomical matter conceals the extraordinary informational density concentrated at its center. The Magician’s body consequently functions as the primary cosmological repository of a Universe perpetually greater than the Actual Universe, establishing a relationship in which an individual organism becomes the central constituent of a cosmic totality whose physical extent surpasses the reality in which that individual was originally born. This reconstruction produces an internal structure that cannot be adequately described using the conventional anatomy of either a human organism or an ordinary celestial body, although its principal regions may be designated the crust, mantle, and core. The outermost crust forms the accessible boundary of the internalized cosmological domain, beyond which lie increasingly severe distortions of spatial continuity and dimensional relationships. Beneath this crust, the mantle contains numerous spatial fault-type supercell distortions comparable to the Walls of Storms surrounding the Lostbelts, although their intensity and structural severity are several times greater. These abnormalities do not consist of ordinary atmospheric disturbances, but of violent discontinuities in spatial coordinates, dimensional orientation, and phase relationships, creating a region in which conventional movement, observation, and spatial transportation cannot be assumed to function normally. An object attempting to penetrate these distortions may encounter incompatible spatial positions, disrupted dimensional connections, or an inability to establish a stable destination within the reconstructed framework. Beyond the mantle lies the core, the deepest domain of Replica Universe and the region in which its accumulated cosmological history, reconstructed celestial contents, and connection to the Sixth Magician are most intensely concentrated. Within this region, it is theorized that the summoning of Servants belonging to Proper Human History is impossible, as the independent historical and metaphysical conditions of Replica Universe do not necessarily provide the spiritual foundations or historical coordinates required for conventional Heroic Spirit summoning. This incompatibility does not imply that the Throne of Heroes has been destroyed, but that the core belongs to a cosmological order whose historical foundation differs fundamentally from the Human Order. The extraordinary constitution of Replica Universe also renders its internal structure almost impossible to analyze through conventional observational mechanisms, as its accumulated informational density exceeds the equivalent of one trillion years of cosmological history. When the Near-Future Observation Lens SHEBA, possessing a temporal observational range of approximately one billion years, is directed toward its interior, the attempt to process such overwhelming information causes the instrument to undergo accelerated deterioration, becoming worn out and eventually ceasing to function. This failure is not the result of a deliberate attack by the Sixth Magician, but the consequence of attempting to observe a cosmological structure whose temporal and informational extent surpasses the capacity of the observer. An examination conducted through the greater computational capabilities of TRISMEGISTUS II produces an even more peculiar result, as the system deliberately refuses to complete its analysis. The Atlas Institute’s safety mechanisms recognize that a sufficiently comprehensive external examination of Replica Universe could reinforce the recognition of its otherwise unfathomable cosmological condition as an established fact, introducing the possibility that the act of successfully verifying such an existence would itself possess dangerous metaphysical consequences. Rather than permit the calculation to reach a definitive conclusion, TRISMEGISTUS II activates its safeguards and terminates the analysis, leaving the complete structure of Replica Universe unresolved. The abnormality is therefore distinguished by two separate observational dangers: an informational density capable of exhausting an inadequate observation mechanism and a cosmological constitution whose successful confirmation may itself alter the conditions under which the phenomenon is recognized. Yet the greatest significance of Replica Universe lies not merely in its dimensional structure or the internalization of its astronomical contents, but in its subsequent development through Retroupdate. After establishing the geocentric reconstruction, the Sixth Magician unlawfully mirrored and duplicated Earth’s potential to create Life, applying that planetary prerogative to the celestial bodies belonging to his independently created cosmos. This process did not merely reproduce terrestrial organisms, but established the conditions through which countless celestial environments could develop their own life-bearing histories according to their respective physical and metaphysical circumstances. Through Retroupdate, the Sixth Magician reconstructed one trillion years of Lost History, encompassing the astronomical development, environmental transformations, biological evolution, and emergence of extraordinary lifeforms throughout Replica Universe. The strongest lifeforms produced by these reconstructed celestial histories were subsequently identified and their defining evolutionary characteristics incorporated into the Magician’s own cosmological existence. This historical reconstruction was followed by the simulation of a virtual future extending twelve trillion years, permitting the development of those celestial environments and their corresponding lifeforms to be examined across an immense projected span of cosmic evolution. Through the incorporation of the simulated future into the replica’s established cosmological history, the Sixth Magician produced an effective developmental framework encompassing thirteen trillion years, combining one trillion years of reconstructed past with twelve trillion years of virtual future. The resulting histories provided the foundation for the assimilation of the ultimate evolutionary characteristics of countless celestial bodies, allowing the Magician to establish a cosmological timeline in which his own existence occupied the position of their strongest and most complete lifeform. Through this artificial reconstruction of planetary life-generating potential, celestial evolution, and cosmological history, the Sixth Magician became the Ultimate One of Countless Celestial Bodies, an existence whose status differs from that of a naturally occurring planetary Ultimate One because it was established through the Sixth Magic rather than through the independent evolution of a single celestial origin. The designation does not imply that the Magician has become the naturally born Ultimate One of every planet within the Actual Universe, but that the Replica Universe possesses an internally valid cosmological history in which the ultimate evolutionary conclusions of its innumerable celestial bodies converge upon him. His connection to Replica Universe consequently transcends the relationship between a creator and an external creation, becoming a form of Universal Existential Integration in which the Magician’s physical manifestation, reconstructed history, assimilated celestial characteristics, and continued existence are inseparably supported by the greater cosmic framework. Although he may retain the appearance and localized anatomy of a human organism, his complete existence can no longer be reduced to the biological structures of that body, for the destruction of its material manifestation does not necessarily constitute the destruction of the independently existing Universe supporting it. The Replica Universe remains established within its fourteenth-dimensional phase, preserving the cosmological foundation through which the Magician’s existence may continue or regain material expression. As a consequence, an opponent possessing sufficient destructive power to annihilate the Actual Earth would remain incapable of eliminating Replica Universe through the application of planetary-scale force alone. Even the destruction of the Magician’s visible body would not automatically eliminate the cosmic structure supporting him, because the fundamental target is no longer an ordinary organism but an independently created Universe of greater extent than the Actual Universe itself. A phenomenon capable of destroying an entire Universe would represent the minimum general category of destructive power necessary to threaten this foundation, although even such an attack would require the ability to interact with the replica’s fourteenth-dimensional existence and overcome the perpetually greater scope of its cosmological structure. This condition does not establish that the Sixth Magician possesses unrestricted omnipotence, nor that Replica Universe exists beyond the Swirl of the Root, since the creation of an independent cosmos does not automatically confer authority over the metaphysical origin of all phenomena. Rather, the extraordinary significance of Replica Universe is that it represents the successful actualization of an entire cosmic totality through True Magic, followed by the reconstruction of that totality into the existential foundation of its creator. It is a Universe whose exterior has become overwhelmingly void, whose interior contains an impossible concentration of celestial structures and accumulated history, whose deepest regions defy conventional observation and the foundations of Proper Human History, and whose central existence has artificially acquired the ultimate evolutionary characteristics of countless celestial bodies. Its continued existence is not contingent upon the physical survival of the Actual Earth, the persistence of an ordinary material body, or the integrity of a single astronomical structure. It is an independently actualized greater cosmos whose totality has been concentrated within the individual responsible for its creation. In this sense, Replica Universe is not merely the supreme creation of the Sixth Magician, but the fundamental basis of what he has become. Where an ordinary human is an individual born within the Universe and sustained by its physical conditions, the Sixth Magician has reversed that relationship, creating a Universe greater than the one in which he was born and subsequently establishing his own existence as the central domain through which that greater cosmos recognizes and maintains the entirety of its celestial contents. The final result is a metaphysical contradiction of extraordinary scale: an apparently finite human existence containing the effective astronomical totality of a Universe that perpetually exceeds the cosmic framework surrounding him. Replica Universe is therefore the miracle by which a Magician ceases to be merely an existence within the Universe and becomes the central existence sustaining a greater Universe of his own creation.

ABILITIES
Universal Cosmogenesis — Creation of a Greater Universe: Universal Cosmogenesis is the fundamental miracle of the Sixth True Magic, granting its practitioner the capacity to create a complete, independently existing Universe encompassing the totality of space, time, matter, energy, celestial bodies, physical laws, causal relationships, and the cosmological principles necessary for the existence of all corresponding phenomena. Unlike Creation Magecraft, which produces or transforms objects within an already established World, the Sixth Magic actualizes the cosmic framework itself, allowing an entirely new Universe to exist without requiring the original Universe to provide its physical matter, spacetime, or energetic foundation. The resulting creation, designated Replica Universe, reproduces the structural totality of the Actual Universe while possessing its own independent spacetime continuum and cosmological development. Its existence is therefore neither an illusion nor a simulation maintained through a computational mechanism, but a genuine cosmic actuality established through a miraculous principle beyond conventional thaumaturgy. The act of creation does not require the Magician to individually manufacture every galaxy, planet, star, or elementary particle through separate applications of Magecraft. Rather, the Sixth Magic actualizes the complete system within which those phenomena can exist, permitting their contents and relationships to become constituents of a unified cosmological structure. This distinguishes Universal Cosmogenesis from ordinary matter creation, dimensional expansion, and the reproduction of a localized World through a Reality Marble. Where conventional Magecraft operates upon the contents of an established reality, the Sixth Magic produces another reality possessing the same fundamental qualification as the original cosmos. The created Universe subsequently becomes the foundation for every other manifestation of the Sixth Magic, including dimensional overlay, celestial materialization, universal reconstruction, and the eventual integration of its totality into the Magician’s own existence.

Perpetual Cosmological Superiority — The Greater Universe: One of the Sixth Magic’s defining properties is the ability to maintain Replica Universe as a cosmos perpetually greater than the Actual Universe from which its original structure was derived. The word replica therefore does not describe a lesser imitation, but the relationship between an original cosmological template and its independently actualized counterpart. The replica is not restricted to the observable portion of the Actual Universe, nor is its total extent determined by the astronomical measurements available to contemporary human civilization. Its cosmological framework encompasses the reproduction of the original Universe while sustaining a greater scope and capacity as an intrinsic condition of its creation. This relationship persists throughout the continued existence of the two universes, preventing the replica from becoming merely an equal-sized copy whose superiority could be lost through subsequent cosmic expansion. The Sixth Magic therefore establishes a persistent asymmetry between the original and its creation. This superiority does not necessarily mean that every individual celestial body inside Replica Universe possesses greater mass, energy, or physical dimensions than its corresponding counterpart. Rather, the greater property belongs to the total cosmological framework, including its spatial extent, capacity for celestial existence, and potential for development. Even after Retroupdate renders ninety-nine percent of its external regions void of their former astronomical contents, the underlying Universe retains its greater cosmological extent. The absence of material objects from an enormous portion of its spacetime does not diminish the scope of the spacetime itself. Consequently, the Sixth Magician’s existential foundation remains connected to a Universe whose totality exceeds that of the Actual Universe, establishing a fundamental distinction between the destruction of ordinary astronomical structures and the elimination of the complete cosmological system supporting his existence.

Fourteenth-Dimensional Existence — Cosmological Overlay: Fourteenth-Dimensional Existence is the ability through which Replica Universe remains independently established while occupying a state of Overlay relative to the Actual Universe. The replica is maintained within a fourteenth-dimensional framework that permits its complete cosmological structure to correspond spatially with the original cosmos without being restricted to the same ordinary physical coordinates. This dimension does not merely represent another direction of conventional three-dimensional movement, but the superior framework through which the Sixth Magic preserves the independence of two otherwise overlapping cosmic totalities. Within this arrangement, Replica Universe possesses genuine spacetime, celestial matter, energy, and physical interactions, although those phenomena do not ordinarily manifest within the same material phase as the Actual Universe. As a result, corresponding celestial bodies can exist in apparent spatial coincidence without colliding or imposing the cumulative gravitational forces that would otherwise result from their superposition. A galaxy belonging to Replica Universe does not need to occupy an additional region of conventional space beyond the galaxies of the Actual Universe, because its position is determined through the replica’s independent cosmological coordinates. Likewise, the creation of a greater Universe does not require the original cosmos to expand in order to accommodate it. The fourteenth-dimensional framework provides the necessary separation between their structures, ensuring that the extraordinary mass and energy contained within Replica Universe do not cause the Actual Universe to collapse beneath their apparent coexistence. This ability also permits the Magician to interact with phenomena belonging to his creation through dimensional and phase relationships inaccessible to ordinary physical observation. Fourteenth-Dimensional Existence is consequently not simply a defensive property, but the structural foundation supporting the simultaneous independence, coexistence, and potential interaction of the two universes.

Phase Existence — Separation of Cosmological Realities: Phase Existence is the condition through which every celestial body and physical phenomenon belonging to Replica Universe maintains genuine actuality while remaining separated from the material framework of the Actual Universe. Within the fourteenth-dimensional Overlay, the contents of Replica Universe exist in a distinct phase-state that preserves their independent physical properties without requiring them to participate in ordinary interactions with the original cosmos. A planet existing in this condition possesses its own material composition, gravitational relationships, internal structure, and position within the replica’s cosmological order, yet it does not necessarily become visible or tangible to an observer restricted to the Actual Universe. The phase-state is therefore fundamentally different from an illusion, spirit form, or object temporarily removed from physical reality. The object remains physically real within its native cosmological framework, while the relationship permitting interaction with the original Universe remains unestablished. This distinction is essential to the Sixth Magic because the creation of Replica Universe would otherwise introduce an impossible concentration of matter and energy into the Actual Universe through ordinary spatial superposition. Phase Existence prevents this conflict by allowing both universes to maintain their internal physical coherence without surrendering their independence. It also provides the basis through which the Magician can manipulate the relationship between manifested and unmanifested celestial structures. A phenomenon can remain genuine without occupying the material phase of the original cosmos, and the alteration of that phase relationship allows its physical manifestation to be controlled without requiring conventional transportation across astronomical distances.

Phase Materialization — Actualization of Celestial Phenomena: Phase Materialization is the ability to convert the phase-state of phenomena belonging to Replica Universe into a condition permitting material interaction with the Actual Universe. Through this process, the Sixth Magician can cause selected portions of his created cosmos to acquire physical manifestation within an external environment while preserving their underlying connection to the fourteenth-dimensional framework. The phenomenon does not require a celestial body to traverse an astronomical distance through conventional space, nor does it require the Magician to construct a duplicate of that body from the matter available at its destination. Instead, the object already exists within Replica Universe, and the Sixth Magic alters the relationship between its native phase and the material framework in which it is to appear. Consequently, astronomical structures, matter, energy, and environmental conditions can become physically accessible without requiring the entire Replica Universe to descend into the Actual Universe. The process can also be reversed, returning a manifested phenomenon to its previous phase relationship and separating it from ordinary physical interaction. Phase Materialization therefore permits the Magician to express the contents of his greater Universe selectively rather than releasing its entire cosmological mass into the original cosmos. Its applications extend from the manifestation of individual objects to the potential expression of far larger celestial phenomena, although the physical consequences of such manifestations depend upon the circumstances in which interaction is established. The Sixth Magic does not transform every materialized object into an indestructible existence, and the destruction of a particular manifestation does not automatically destroy the corresponding cosmological structure sustaining it. The original phase-domain remains distinct from the local physical expression, allowing the Magician to separate the loss of a manifested phenomenon from the continued existence of its source within Replica Universe.

Retroupdate — Universal Reconstruction: Retroupdate is the principal reconstructive ability of the Sixth True Magic, permitting the Sixth Magician to resimulate, remodel, and update the entirety of Replica Universe according to a revised cosmological arrangement. The phenomenon extends beyond ordinary reality alteration because its target is not a localized object, environment, or physical law, but the comprehensive system through which the replica establishes its celestial distribution, spacetime relationships, and historical development. Through Retroupdate, planets, stars, galaxies, and the empty space separating them can be reorganized as constituents of a single Universe Update without requiring each celestial body to physically travel along an ordinary trajectory. The process operates by reconstructing the cosmological model governing the existence and relationships of those phenomena, allowing their positions, phases, and associated historical conditions to be reassigned within the replica’s independent framework. Its retroactive character arises from the ability to establish not merely a revised present arrangement, but the internal historical conditions necessary for that arrangement to possess validity within Replica Universe. A new cosmological state can therefore be accompanied by a reconstructed developmental foundation, rather than existing as an inexplicable alteration imposed upon an unchanged past. This does not require the Actual Universe to undergo corresponding changes, since the operation is performed upon the independent cosmic framework created by the Sixth Magic. Retroupdate consequently differs from ordinary time travel, which changes temporal position, and from the Second Magic’s operation of parallel worlds, because it reconstructs an already actualized Universe under the direct authority of its creator. Its most extraordinary application is the transformation of the replica into a geocentric cosmological structure centered upon the Sixth Magician’s own body.

Retroactive Cosmological Resimulation — Reconstruction of Cosmic History: Retroactive Cosmological Resimulation is the historical component of Retroupdate, allowing the Sixth Magic to calculate and reconstruct the developmental conditions associated with a particular cosmic arrangement. Ordinarily, the present distribution of celestial bodies is the result of an immense sequence of preceding physical events, including cosmic expansion, gravitational collapse, stellar evolution, galactic formation, and the interactions of matter and energy across astronomical timescales. Altering the present structure of a Universe would not automatically provide a coherent historical explanation for the revised condition. Retroupdate overcomes this discrepancy by establishing a corresponding reconstructed history within Replica Universe, permitting the new cosmic arrangement to possess its own internally valid developmental foundation. This ability does not simply rewrite memories, alter historical documents, or move celestial bodies backward through time. It reconstructs the conditions through which the Universe recognizes a particular arrangement as belonging to its own cosmological development. The resulting history can include astronomical events and evolutionary outcomes that were never physically experienced by the Actual Universe, because the replica possesses an independent historical framework. Through this mechanism, the Sixth Magician can establish immense periods of Lost History and simulated future development without requiring the original cosmos to undergo an equivalent chronological sequence. The ability is especially significant because it transforms historical development into a component of the Magician’s reconstructive authority. The Sixth Magic can produce not merely a new arrangement of celestial matter, but the accumulated cosmological circumstances through which that arrangement becomes an established fact within its created Universe.

Cosmic Canopy — Isolation of the Universal Reference Point: The Cosmic Canopy is a specialized manifestation of the Sixth Magic that permits the Magician to obstruct the contact between his own body and everything outside a designated enclosed domain. Unlike an ordinary bounded field designed to repel physical attacks or conceal magical activity, the canopy interferes with the spatial and informational relationships through which Replica Universe distinguishes the Magician’s body from the surrounding cosmos. By preventing external contact, the canopy establishes an artificial condition in which the replica’s cosmological recognition system cannot correctly identify the separation between its central subject and the astronomical structures existing beyond that subject. This was the mechanism through which the Sixth Magician induced the decisive Retroupdate that transformed his creation. Once the canopy completely isolated his body, Replica Universe was made to recognize the entirety of its celestial contents as already residing within the enclosed domain. The distinction between the Magician and the external Universe was consequently disrupted at the level of cosmological reference, producing an apparent contradiction that the replica attempted to resolve through Universal Reconstruction. The canopy’s function was therefore not to physically drag celestial bodies into the Magician or to withstand the gravitational weight of a Universe through material resistance. It manipulated the conditions under which the replica interpreted the location of its own contents. Its significance lies in its capacity to produce a universal-scale consequence through the deliberate obstruction of a localized relationship. Following the completed Universe Update, the cosmological reconstruction remains established independently of the continued presence of the original canopy, because Retroupdate has already actualized the revised arrangement as part of Replica Universe’s own structure.

Geocentric Retroupdate — Universal Centralization: Geocentric Retroupdate is the defining transformation through which the Sixth Magician established his own body as the central reference point of Replica Universe. Following the activation of the Cosmic Canopy, the replica interpreted all of its planets, stars, galaxies, and other celestial contents as already residing within the Magician’s enclosed existence. Retroupdate subsequently reconstructed the Universe to satisfy that interpretation, replacing its formerly distributed astronomical arrangement with a geocentric structure in which the Magician’s body became the central domain containing its celestial totality. This operation did not impose the historical geocentric model upon the Actual Universe, nor did it cause the physical Earth to occupy the center of all observable space. The term describes the internal organization of Replica Universe following the reconstruction of its coordinates, phase relationships, and cosmological reference system. The Magician’s body was established as the primary location through which the replica recognized the existence of its astronomical contents, while the corresponding external regions were rendered void. The resulting condition was not achieved through ordinary gravitational attraction or the physical compression of innumerable stars into a human body. Instead, the fourteenth-dimensional framework permitted the celestial structures to be reassigned through their phase relationships, allowing their actual existence to remain intact without imposing their combined mass upon the material organism. Geocentric Retroupdate consequently transformed the Magician from the external creator of a Universe into its central cosmological constituent, establishing the essential relationship upon which his subsequent physiology, durability, and composite Ultimate One status depend.

Celestial Internalization — The Universe Within the Body: Celestial Internalization is the consequence of Geocentric Retroupdate through which the entirety of Replica Universe’s celestial contents becomes concentrated within the phase-domain associated with the Sixth Magician’s body. The phenomenon does not operate according to ordinary physical volume, because the body’s apparent dimensions do not determine the size of the fourteenth-dimensional cosmological region connected to it. From the perspective of conventional biological observation, the Magician continues to possess a finite material form. From the perspective of Replica Universe, that form is the central location containing the reconstructed relationships and astronomical contents of an independently existing greater cosmos. The stars, planets, galaxies, and intervening structures do not cease to exist merely because their external locations have been emptied. They remain constituents of Replica Universe, but their positions are now defined through the internal cosmological framework associated with the Magician’s existence. As a result, the Magician effectively contains a Universe greater than the Actual Universe without requiring his body to possess an equivalent conventional mass or volume. This makes Celestial Internalization fundamentally different from possessing an enormous storage space, a dimensional pocket, or a Reality Marble containing a miniature world. The body is not simply holding a collection of astronomical objects. It has become the central structure through which the Replica Universe establishes the existence of its entire material totality. The connection also transforms the significance of the Magician’s physical survival, because the body is no longer an organism whose existence can be understood independently of the Universe concentrated within it.

Universal Hollowing — The Ninety-Nine Percent Void: Universal Hollowing is the large-scale cosmological consequence of Retroupdate through which approximately ninety-nine percent of Replica Universe’s exterior becomes void of its original celestial contents. This phenomenon is not the complete destruction of ninety-nine percent of the Universe, but the removal of the astronomical structures previously occupying those regions through their reassignment to the Magician’s internal phase-domain. The surrounding spacetime framework continues to exist, retaining the cosmological extent and dimensional relationships established through Universal Cosmogenesis. However, its previous arrangement of celestial matter is no longer distributed throughout the majority of that space. Instead, the celestial contents are concentrated around the central domain identified with the Sixth Magician’s body. The resulting Universe possesses an extraordinary discrepancy between its immense external emptiness and the overwhelming information density of its interior. An observer attempting to examine its outer regions might conclude that the replica has lost most of its astronomical substance, yet the supposed absence is misleading because those contents have not been annihilated. Their existence has been transferred into a different arrangement through Retroupdate. Universal Hollowing therefore represents the spatial counterpart of Celestial Internalization. One phenomenon empties the exterior while the other concentrates the celestial totality within the Magician. The Replica Universe remains perpetually greater than the Actual Universe throughout this process, demonstrating that the reduction of its external material distribution does not diminish the independent cosmological framework sustaining it.

Universal Existential Integration — The Magician and Cosmos: Universal Existential Integration is the ability through which the Sixth Magician becomes inseparably connected to Replica Universe as the fundamental basis of his own continued existence. Prior to the completion of Retroupdate, the Magician could be understood as an individual possessing the capacity to create and operate an independent Universe. Following Geocentric Retroupdate, that relationship was transformed. The Universe’s celestial totality was concentrated within his body’s phase-domain, and his existence became the central reference through which the replica maintained its reconstructed cosmological arrangement. The distinction between the practitioner and his creation consequently ceased to be a simple relationship of external ownership. The Magician’s material body remained an identifiable physical organism, but his complete existence now included the independent cosmological foundation supporting that organism. In practical terms, an opponent attempting to destroy him must distinguish between damaging his local manifestation and eliminating the Replica Universe through which his existence persists. The destruction of his ordinary biological structure does not automatically destroy the cosmological framework connected to it, just as the destruction of a manifested celestial phenomenon does not necessarily destroy the phase-domain from which it originated. Universal Existential Integration therefore establishes a form of existential continuity far beyond conventional biological immortality. The Magician remains an individual, but the foundation supporting that individuality is no longer confined to an ordinary organism, soul container, or localized spiritual structure. It is a complete Universe whose existence is independent of the original cosmos.

Cosmological Immortality — Indestructibility of the Universal Foundation: Cosmological Immortality is the extraordinary resistance to permanent destruction acquired by the Sixth Magician through Universal Existential Integration. Unlike conventional immortality, which may depend upon regenerative biology, the preservation of the soul, resurrection mechanisms, or the restoration of physical structures, this condition derives from the continued existence of Replica Universe itself. The Magician’s ordinary material form can no longer be treated as the entirety of his existential foundation, because the complete basis of his existence has been incorporated into an independently actualized greater cosmos. Consequently, a phenomenon capable of destroying the Actual Earth does not possess sufficient destructive significance to eliminate Replica Universe merely through its planetary-scale effects. Even the complete destruction of the Magician’s apparent physical body would not necessarily establish his death, because the underlying Universe remains intact within its fourteenth-dimensional framework. The destruction of the complete entity requires the destruction or fundamental negation of that cosmological foundation. An opponent would therefore require at least a phenomenon capable of threatening an entire Universe, rather than one restricted to the annihilation of individual planets or stars. Furthermore, because Replica Universe remains greater than the Actual Universe and occupies a separate dimensional phase, possessing the energy necessary to destroy the original cosmos would not automatically guarantee successful interaction with the replica. Cosmological Immortality does not derive from the assertion that every physical component of the Magician is infinitely durable. It derives from the fact that destroying a localized component is categorically different from destroying the complete cosmic existence supporting it.

Cosmological Reconstitution — Restoration of Material Manifestation: Cosmological Reconstitution is the capacity for the Sixth Magician’s material existence to remain recoverable through the continued integrity of Replica Universe. When a conventional organism suffers catastrophic physical destruction, its survival depends upon whether its biological or spiritual mechanisms can reverse the damage before the conditions required for life are permanently lost. The Sixth Magician’s condition is fundamentally different because his complete existence is not terminated by the destruction of an individual manifestation. So long as the Replica Universe persists, the cosmic foundation supporting his identity remains established, and the material expression of that identity can be restored through the same phase relationships connecting his physical body to the greater cosmological structure. This process does not require the reconstruction of the entire Universe following every injury, because the Universe itself has not necessarily been damaged. Rather, a destroyed or damaged material manifestation may be reexpressed from a still-existing cosmological foundation. The process resembles regeneration only from the perspective of an external observer who witnesses the return of a physical body after its destruction. Metaphysically, it is the restoration of a local manifestation belonging to an existence that never ceased to persist. This ability is consequently distinct from ordinary cellular regeneration and from the Third Magic’s materialization of the soul. It does not require every cell of the Magician’s body to independently possess the functions of the complete organism. The continuity of existence is instead maintained through the greater Universe with which the Magician has become integrated.

Spatial Fault Supercells — The Mantle of Distorted Space: Spatial Fault Supercells are extraordinary environmental distortions existing beneath the crust-like exterior of Replica Universe’s internal structure. These phenomena resemble the Walls of Storms surrounding the Celestial Bodies, although their severity is several times greater by comparison. They are not conventional atmospheric disturbances, but abnormalities affecting spatial continuity, dimensional relationships, and the stability of phase coordinates. An object attempting to penetrate the region may encounter distorted distances, unstable spatial orientation, and interruptions in the correspondence between physical movement and dimensional position. Because the supercells belong to the reconstructed interior of Replica Universe, their behavior is governed by the cosmological conditions established through Retroupdate rather than solely by the ordinary physics of the Actual Universe. Their presence creates a formidable obstacle to physical intrusion, dimensional transportation, and remote observation. A mechanism capable of moving through ordinary space cannot necessarily traverse the supercells by following a conventional route, because the spatial relationships required to establish that route may themselves become unstable. Likewise, an ability designed to bypass physical distance must still identify a valid destination within the relevant phase framework. The supercells therefore serve as an internal defensive environment associated with the Magician’s cosmological anatomy, protecting the deeper regions of Replica Universe from straightforward penetration. They are not simply barriers of magical energy that can be exhausted through ordinary attrition, but structural abnormalities embedded within the greater Universe’s reconstructed spatial order.

Proper Human History Exclusion — Incompatibility of Heroic Spirit Summoning: Proper Human History Exclusion is the condition observed within the deepest regions of Replica Universe, where the reconstructed cosmological history is incompatible with the ordinary foundations required for summoning Servants associated with Proper Human History. Conventional Heroic Spirit summoning depends upon establishing a connection between the summoning system, the relevant spiritual foundation, and the historical records associated with the intended Heroic Spirit. The central domain of Replica Universe, however, possesses an independent cosmic history extending far beyond the ordinary chronological structure of humanity’s development. Its trillion-year reconstructed Lost History and twelve-trillion-year virtual future do not belong to the same historical framework through which Proper Human History maintains its established summoning conditions. Consequently, it is theorized that attempting to summon a Servant of Proper Human History within the core would fail because the necessary historical and metaphysical coordinates cannot be properly established. This does not mean the Sixth Magician has destroyed the Throne of Heroes or erased the Heroic Spirits associated with humanity. Rather, the internal conditions of Replica Universe do not provide the ordinary foundation required for such a summoning to be completed. The phenomenon is therefore one of cosmological incompatibility rather than conventional anti-summoning Magecraft. An invocation that operates successfully within the Human Order cannot automatically be assumed to function within the central region of an independently reconstructed Universe whose historical foundation is not established through the same system.

Trans-Temporal Information Density — One Trillion Years of Cosmological Information: Trans-Temporal Information Density is the extraordinary condition produced by the concentration of Replica Universe’s celestial structures and reconstructed history within the Magician’s internal cosmological domain. The information contained within this region exceeds the equivalent of one trillion years of cosmic development, incorporating astronomical configurations, historical relationships, environmental evolution, and the accumulated consequences of the replica’s reconstructed existence. Ordinarily, the information associated with the history of a Universe is distributed throughout its vast spatial and temporal structure. Following Retroupdate, however, the replica’s celestial contents and historical foundations have been concentrated into the phase-domain associated with a single central existence. The resulting information density is therefore disproportionately greater than anything suggested by the Magician’s visible physical dimensions. A conventional observer encountering his material body would not be examining an ordinary human organism alone, but the interface of a cosmological structure containing an extraordinary quantity of temporal information. This ability is not equivalent to automatic omniscience. The possession of information within the Magician’s cosmological foundation does not necessarily mean that every detail is continuously present within his conscious awareness. Its significance lies in the amount of objective cosmological content incorporated into his existence and the extreme demands imposed upon mechanisms attempting to reconstruct that content through observation.

Observational Time Erosion — The Failure of SHEBA: Observational Time Erosion is a consequence of the extraordinary information density within Replica Universe, demonstrated through the failure of an observation mechanism such as the Near-Future Observation Lens SHEBA. In this original continuity, SHEBA possesses a temporal observation range of approximately one billion years, a capacity sufficient for extraordinary examinations of cosmic phenomena but inadequate for the internal structure of Replica Universe. When directed toward the Magician’s cosmological domain, the instrument encounters information corresponding to more than one trillion years of accumulated history. The act of observation therefore requires the mechanism to process a temporal structure vastly exceeding its permissible operating capacity. Rather than simply returning an incomplete image or an error message, SHEBA undergoes accelerated deterioration as the demands of observation overwhelm its temporal foundation. Its mechanism becomes worn out and eventually ceases functioning, as though the effort of examining Replica Universe has forced it beyond the duration for which it was designed to remain operational. This phenomenon does not require the Magician to consciously attack the instrument or activate a defensive spell against it. The failure occurs because the observer attempts to process a cosmological structure whose informational density exceeds its own observational limits. Observational Time Erosion consequently constitutes a passive danger to insufficiently equipped investigative systems, demonstrating that even the acquisition of knowledge concerning the Sixth Magician may impose consequences beyond ordinary mechanical or computational failure.

Cosmological Verification Hazard — The Refusal of TRISMEGISTUS II: The Cosmological Verification Hazard is a metaphysical danger arising from the possibility that an independent observer could establish the extraordinary structure of Replica Universe as a more firmly recognized fact. This phenomenon is illustrated by the deliberate refusal of TRISMEGISTUS II to complete an analysis of the Magician’s internal cosmology. Unlike SHEBA, whose failure results from attempting to process information beyond its temporal observation capacity, TRISMEGISTUS II possesses safeguards capable of identifying calculations whose completion may produce unacceptable consequences. When confronted with the Replica Universe, the computational system determines that successfully constructing a complete theoretical model could reinforce the external recognition of the cosmological abnormality. Within the relevant metaphysical framework, independently confirming an otherwise unfathomable phenomenon may contribute to the strength with which that phenomenon is established relative to the observer’s reality. The danger is therefore not simply that the computer might malfunction, but that successfully understanding the structure could provide an additional basis for its recognition as an objective condition. TRISMEGISTUS II accordingly terminates the calculation before producing a complete answer, activating the Atlas Institute’s safety measures. The refusal does not imply that Replica Universe lacks genuine existence prior to observation. Rather, it indicates that external verification may possess consequences beyond the ordinary acquisition of information. This makes the Magician’s cosmological existence dangerous to investigate even through systems possessing extraordinary computational capabilities, because the completion of the analysis may affect the relationship between the replica and the reality attempting to comprehend it.

Lost History Reconstruction — One Trillion Years of Cosmic Development: Lost History Reconstruction is the ability through which the Sixth Magician employs Retroupdate to establish a comprehensive record of one trillion years of cosmological development within Replica Universe. The reconstructed history encompasses the formation and destruction of celestial bodies, the evolution of cosmic environments, and the emergence of lifeforms under the physical conditions associated with those environments. Unlike ordinary historical observation, the process does not merely retrieve records of events that have already occurred within the Actual Universe. Instead, it resimulates and establishes a developmental history belonging to the independent cosmological framework of the replica. The resulting record is valid within that Universe because Retroupdate provides the conditions through which the reconstructed developments become part of its established historical structure. This is especially significant for the Magician’s subsequent transformation, since the reconstruction includes the evolutionary histories of countless celestial bodies and the strongest lifeforms produced through their development. The Magician can therefore identify and incorporate the ultimate evolutionary conclusions of those histories without requiring the Actual Universe to have independently experienced one trillion years of equivalent events. The resulting information is condensed into the central cosmological domain associated with his body, contributing to the extraordinary temporal density of his internal existence. Lost History Reconstruction is consequently not merely a means of acquiring astronomical knowledge. It is a method of producing the historical and evolutionary foundation through which the Magician’s ultimate constitution becomes possible.

Virtual Future Simulation — Twelve Trillion Years of Possibility: Virtual Future Simulation is the ability to calculate and establish a projected cosmological development extending twelve trillion years beyond the reconstructed historical foundation of Replica Universe. Through this function, the Sixth Magic extends the outcomes of one trillion years of Lost History into an immense virtual future, simulating the subsequent development of celestial bodies, environmental systems, and the lifeforms associated with them. The process does not require twelve trillion years to elapse in the Actual Universe, nor does it depend upon transporting the Magician physically into the future. Instead, the simulation is performed within the independent cosmological framework of Replica Universe, whose structure can be reconstructed through Retroupdate. The resulting projection encompasses the potential developmental outcomes of countless celestial environments, including the ultimate evolutionary characteristics of the strongest lifeforms that emerge under their respective conditions. Once established, the virtual future can be incorporated into the replica’s valid cosmological history through Retroupdate, permitting its results to contribute to the Magician’s current existential constitution. The ability therefore transcends ordinary prediction, because its significance does not end with calculating what might eventually occur. It establishes the conditions through which the projected evolutionary results become relevant to the present structure of Replica Universe. By combining one trillion years of reconstructed history with twelve trillion years of simulated future development, the Sixth Magician obtains an effective developmental framework spanning thirteen trillion years. This enormous historical structure provides the foundation for the assimilation of countless ultimate lifeforms and the establishment of the Magician’s composite Ultimate One status.

Planetary Life-Potential Replication — Unlawful Mirroring of Earth’s Genesis: Planetary Life-Potential Replication is the extraordinary application of Retroupdate through which the Sixth Magician unlawfully duplicates Earth’s capacity to generate Life and establishes equivalent potential across the celestial environments of Replica Universe. The process does not simply reproduce existing terrestrial organisms or manufacture artificial biological structures through ordinary alchemy. Instead, it mirrors the underlying planetary potential through which life can arise and develop, incorporating that capacity into the reconstructed histories of other celestial bodies. In TYPE-MOON’s metaphysics, the relationship between a celestial body and the lifeforms associated with it extends beyond ordinary physical composition, involving the planet’s own existential foundation and the possibility of producing a highest-ranking representative. The Sixth Magician appropriates this relationship through the reconstruction of his created Universe, establishing conditions in which countless celestial bodies can possess a life-generating developmental foundation. The resulting lifeforms need not resemble terrestrial organisms, because their evolution is determined through the physical and metaphysical conditions associated with their respective celestial environments. The process is considered unlawful because the Magician reproduces a planetary prerogative through an artificial cosmological mechanism rather than receiving it through the natural development of an independent celestial origin. This ability permits the Replica Universe to generate an enormous diversity of biological and existential outcomes, establishing the necessary foundation for identifying the strongest lifeforms associated with countless celestial bodies. Its significance is therefore not merely the multiplication of life, but the reproduction of the conditions through which celestial bodies can produce their own ultimate representatives.

Ultimate Evolutionary Assimilation — Integration of the Strongest Lifeforms: Ultimate Evolutionary Assimilation is the process through which the Sixth Magician incorporates the defining characteristics of the strongest lifeforms arising from the reconstructed and simulated histories of Replica Universe. The ability operates through the combination of Retroupdate, Planetary Life-Potential Replication, and the thirteen-trillion-year developmental framework established through Lost History and Virtual Future Simulation. Each eligible celestial environment contributes its own evolutionary conditions, and the strongest lifeforms emerging from those conditions provide the ultimate characteristics associated with that particular history. The Magician subsequently assimilates those characteristics into his own reconstructed existential constitution. This is fundamentally different from ordinary biological transplantation, genetic modification, or the imitation of an opponent’s abilities through conventional Magecraft. The traits are incorporated as the developmental outcomes of the replica’s own established cosmological history, allowing the Magician’s existence to reflect the evolutionary conclusions of countless celestial origins. The resulting composite constitution may encompass extraordinary environmental adaptation, unconventional biological structure, and existential properties foreign to terrestrial life, insofar as those properties belong to the assimilated ultimate lifeforms. However, the process does not automatically grant the Magician every unrelated ability possessed by every supernatural being in the Actual Universe. Its source is the collection of ultimate evolutionary outcomes established within Replica Universe. The significance of the assimilation lies in the union of numerous celestial developmental conclusions into a single existence, producing a being whose physiological foundation can no longer be classified according to the ordinary evolutionary history of one planet.

Composite Ultimate One — Ultimate One of Countless Celestial Bodies: Composite Ultimate One is the culminating transformation through which the Sixth Magician becomes the artificially established Ultimate One of countless celestial bodies within Replica Universe. The condition results from the unlawful duplication of Earth’s life-generating potential, the reconstruction of one trillion years of Lost History, and the simulation of twelve trillion years of virtual future development. Through these processes, the Magician establishes a cosmological timeline in which the strongest lifeforms arising from innumerable celestial environments contribute their defining characteristics to his own existence. Retroupdate subsequently actualizes the resulting configuration, making the Magician the ultimate representative of the celestial bodies whose evolutionary histories have been incorporated into the replica. This designation is not merely a declaration of immense combat ability. Within TYPE-MOON terminology, an Ultimate One represents a fundamental relationship with a celestial origin, and the Sixth Magician has manufactured a cosmological framework in which that relationship is established across countless bodies simultaneously. His status is therefore artificial in its method of acquisition but genuine within the historical and metaphysical order of Replica Universe. The transformation does not mean that he has become the naturally born Ultimate One of every planet in the Actual Universe, nor that every independent TYPE has been assimilated or replaced. Instead, he occupies the ultimate position established by the reconstructed development of his own cosmos. The resulting condition makes him a singular composite existence whose foundation encompasses the evolutionary conclusions of innumerable celestial origins, greatly exceeding the ordinary classification of a terrestrial organism or the naturally occurring supreme representative of a single celestial body.

Alien Celestial Constitution — Physiology Beyond Terrestrial Common Sense: Alien Celestial Constitution is the extraordinary physiological condition resulting from the Magician’s assimilation of ultimate lifeforms belonging to countless distinct celestial environments. Because the Replica Universe reproduces and reconstructs the life-generating potential of numerous celestial bodies, the resulting developmental histories may produce organisms whose fundamental biological properties differ radically from those of terrestrial life. Through Ultimate Evolutionary Assimilation, the Magician incorporates those characteristics into his own cosmological constitution, making the ordinary physical common sense of Earth an inadequate framework for evaluating his complete nature. This does not require him to permanently abandon a human physical appearance, since his visible body remains a local material manifestation of the greater existence integrated with Replica Universe. However, the underlying constitution supporting that manifestation is no longer exclusively derived from the conditions governing ordinary human biology. His existence incorporates the developmental conclusions of lifeforms adapted to environments, physical interactions, and cosmic conditions outside the evolutionary history of Earth. As with naturally occurring Ultimate Ones, the resulting constitution cannot necessarily be assessed using terrestrial assumptions concerning biological limitations or the ordinary relationship between injury and death. Yet its most decisive property remains Universal Existential Integration, because the Magician’s continued existence is supported by the Replica Universe rather than by the survival of a particular arrangement of cells or organs. The alien characteristics of his assimilated physiology supplement that cosmological foundation, establishing an organism whose apparent humanity conceals an extraordinarily composite celestial origin.

Cosmological Authority — Operation of the Replica Universe: Cosmological Authority is the collective capacity through which the Sixth Magician operates upon the independently created Universe that forms the foundation of his existence. This ability derives not from unrestricted dominion over every possible reality, but from his unique relationship as the creator, central reference point, and integrated constituent of Replica Universe. Through that relationship, the Magician can initiate Retroupdate, reconstruct astronomical arrangements, alter the phase relationships of cosmic phenomena, and determine the conditions under which portions of his creation acquire material manifestation. The scale of the domain subject to these operations is the complete Replica Universe, a cosmological framework perpetually greater than the Actual Universe. Consequently, the effects available through Cosmological Authority are not restricted to the manipulation of individual objects or localized environments. The Magician possesses a mechanism capable of reorganizing the relationships between entire celestial structures as elements of a single universal system. Nevertheless, the authority exercised through the Sixth Magic differs from the Divine Authorities of gods and the powers of naturally occurring planetary representatives. It is grounded in the miraculous creation of an independent cosmological framework, rather than in a pre-existing divine right over the original World. The Magician can operate upon his own Universe because the Sixth Magic establishes the principle through which that Universe exists and can be reconstructed. His ability to impose those operations upon the Actual Universe depends upon the interaction between the two frameworks, especially the use of Phase Materialization. This distinction preserves the extraordinary scope of the Sixth Magic without equating its creator with the unrestricted source of all phenomena.

Cosmological Environmental Imposition — Manifestation of the Replica’s Physical Order: Cosmological Environmental Imposition is a potential large-scale application of Phase Materialization through which the Sixth Magician can bring the physical conditions of selected regions of Replica Universe into interaction with the Actual Universe. Because the replica possesses its own astronomical structures, matter, energy, and governing physical relationships, the Magician can use the phase-state of those phenomena to establish an external manifestation of environments originating within his created cosmos. Such manifestations may involve celestial matter, altered spatial arrangements, or environmental conditions that would not ordinarily arise within the corresponding region of the Actual Universe. The mechanism differs from the projection of an individual’s mental landscape through a Reality Marble, because the source is a genuinely existing Universe rather than a personal internal world temporarily imposed upon external reality. It also differs from the passive leakage of an alien environment associated with certain Ultimate Ones, because the Sixth Magic operates through deliberate control of the phase relationship between two independent cosmic frameworks. Once a selected phenomenon is materialized, its interactions with the Actual Universe become consequences of the established overlap. The ability therefore provides a means of expressing the physical order of Replica Universe beyond its own fourteenth-dimensional framework without requiring the complete Universe to become materially present. It does not automatically mean that every physical law of the Actual Universe is permanently replaced, because the scope of the manifestation depends upon the phase relationship actually established. The defining feature is the controlled expression of another genuine cosmic environment within the material domain of the original cosmos.

Universal-Scale Existential Defense — The Greater Cosmos as the True Foundation: Universal-Scale Existential Defense is the ultimate protective consequence of the Sixth Magician’s connection to Replica Universe. An ordinary organism may possess formidable physical durability, supernatural regeneration, or conceptual protection, yet its survival remains dependent upon some identifiable existential foundation. In the Sixth Magician’s case, that foundation is an entire independently created Universe. Consequently, the destruction of a planet, star, or localized region of spacetime cannot automatically eliminate the Magician, even if the attack possesses enough power to annihilate his visible material form. The fundamental target is no longer a human organism alone, but the greater cosmological framework with which that organism has become inseparably integrated. An attacker capable of destroying the Actual Earth would remain unable to destroy Replica Universe merely by applying an equivalent destructive phenomenon to the Magician’s physical location. Even a phenomenon capable of threatening the entirety of the Actual Universe would need to establish interaction with the replica’s separate fourteenth-dimensional foundation, and would confront a cosmos whose total extent remains greater than that of its original counterpart. This defensive condition is not a conventional barrier that prevents every attack from making contact. A weapon may injure the local material body, and an extraordinary supernatural effect may interfere with a manifested phenomenon, but neither accomplishment automatically reaches the true existential foundation. The Magician’s survival is secured by the continued integrity of the Replica Universe, making complete destruction a fundamentally cosmological problem rather than a question of overwhelming ordinary biological durability.

Universe-Level Persistence — Existence Beyond Planetary Destruction: Universe-Level Persistence is the condition through which the Sixth Magician remains supported by Replica Universe even when the material environment in which he appears suffers catastrophic destruction. Because the replica possesses an independent spacetime framework, its continued existence does not require the survival of the Actual Earth, the solar system, or any particular astronomical structure belonging to the original cosmos. The Magician’s connection to that framework consequently grants him a foundation of existence that is independent of ordinary planetary continuity. This does not necessarily mean that he is unaffected by every event occurring within the Actual Universe, but it means that such events do not automatically determine whether his complete existence continues. The destruction of his surroundings may eliminate the conditions supporting an ordinary human body, yet the Magician’s total constitution remains integrated with a self-sustaining greater Universe. The distinction becomes especially significant when considering attacks designed to destroy an enemy by annihilating the environment sustaining them. For the Sixth Magician, the relevant sustaining environment is no longer limited to the physical location in which his material body appears. It is Replica Universe itself. Thus, an attack capable of exterminating all life upon Earth would not necessarily interfere with the continued existence of the Magician, because the cosmic foundation preserving him is separate from the terrestrial environment being destroyed. His persistence is not granted by immunity to the physical consequences of planetary destruction, but by the fact that those consequences do not extend automatically to his independent cosmological foundation.

Universal Self-Actualization — The Completion of the Sixth Magician: Universal Self-Actualization is the final and most comprehensive consequence of the Sixth True Magic, representing the completed union of Universal Cosmogenesis, Retroupdate, Celestial Internalization, Lost History Reconstruction, Virtual Future Simulation, and Composite Ultimate One assimilation. Initially, the Sixth Magician is an individual capable of creating a greater Universe. Through the Cosmic Canopy and Geocentric Retroupdate, he reconstructs that Universe so that its celestial contents become concentrated within the phase-domain of his own body. Through the unlawful duplication of Earth’s life-generating potential, he subsequently establishes the evolutionary histories of countless celestial environments. By reconstructing one trillion years of Lost History and simulating twelve trillion years of future development, he identifies and assimilates the strongest lifeforms associated with those histories, creating a cosmological timeline in which he becomes the Ultimate One of innumerable celestial bodies. The completed result is an existence whose physiology, cosmological authority, historical foundation, and survival are all inseparably connected to Replica Universe. The Magician is no longer merely the external operator of an extraordinary supernatural phenomenon, nor is the replica merely a separate object belonging to him. His individual existence has become the central condition through which the greater Universe maintains its reconstructed celestial totality. Nevertheless, this transformation does not establish that he is identical to Akasha or possesses unrestricted omnipotence over every possible reality. His accomplishment is specific and immense: he has independently created a cosmos greater than the Actual Universe, reconstructed its totality around his own body, and actualized himself as the ultimate lifeform of its countless celestial origins. His physical appearance remains only the most accessible manifestation of a far greater existence.

COMPOSITE ULTIMATE ONE ABILITIES
Composite Ultimate One — Supreme Existence of Countless Celestial Bodies: Composite Ultimate One is the extraordinary existential classification acquired by Avesta Lorsing Manich following the completion of Retroupdate, through which he became the artificial ultimate representative of countless celestial bodies contained within Replica Universe. Unlike an ordinary Ultimate One, whose existence is associated with the supreme lifeform of an individual planet or corresponding celestial region, Avesta possesses a composite constitution established through the convergence of innumerable celestial evolutionary histories into a single organism. By unlawfully reproducing Earth’s potential to create Life across the celestial bodies of Replica Universe, reconstructing one trillion years of Lost History, and simulating twelve trillion years of future development, Avesta established a cosmological timeline in which the strongest evolutionary representatives of those celestial environments were identified and their defining properties incorporated into his own existence. This assimilation encompasses not merely biological characteristics, but the physical, spiritual, conceptual, and supernatural faculties developed by those ultimate lifeforms, including the authority-like functions legitimately associated with their celestial origins. His classification as a Composite Ultimate One is therefore not simply a designation acknowledging his possession of extraordinary physical strength. It describes an existence whose fundamental constitution incorporates the culminating developmental characteristics of countless independent celestial systems. These properties coexist within the unified cosmological foundation maintained by the Sixth Magic, allowing Avesta to retain an individually recognizable identity despite possessing an extraordinarily complex composite physiology. Although he continues to resemble a human in his ordinary manifestation, the nature of his body is no longer adequately described through the evolutionary history of one planet. He has become the collective culmination of an immense artificial cosmic ecosystem, an existence simultaneously representing the strongest lifeforms produced by innumerable celestial histories. Where a conventional Ultimate One embodies the supremacy of a particular celestial origin, Avesta embodies the convergence of countless such supremacies within the independently created Universe supporting his existence.

Alien Common-Sense Transcendence — Existence Beyond Terrestrial Laws: Alien Common-Sense Transcendence is an intrinsic characteristic of Avesta’s Composite Ultimate One physiology, arising from the fact that his constitution is no longer founded exclusively upon the biological, physical, or conceptual principles governing terrestrial life. In TYPE-MOON’s metaphysics, Ultimate Ones are extraordinary extraterrestrial existences that cannot necessarily be judged according to the common sense of Earth. Their structures are fundamentally foreign to ordinary terrestrial organisms, and the concepts through which earthly life experiences damage, mortality, and biological limitation do not automatically possess the same significance when applied to them. Avesta inherits this alien character through the assimilation of the supreme evolutionary traits of countless celestial bodies, each potentially possessing its own physical environment, developmental foundation, and principles of biological existence. As a consequence, attempts to evaluate his complete constitution according to ordinary human anatomy or the conceptual conditions governing terrestrial life are inherently incomplete. Magecraft designed to interfere with human physiology, spiritual foundations dependent upon Earth’s biological classifications, and conceptual effects requiring an ordinary terrestrial lifeform as their subject cannot automatically assume that Avesta satisfies their necessary conditions. His human appearance does not establish that his body possesses the corresponding human weaknesses, because the material form represents only the accessible expression of a far more extensive composite organism. However, this property is not equivalent to transcendence over every possible law or metaphysical principle. Rather, it signifies the genuine foreignness of his existence relative to Earth’s established order. Avesta may participate in terrestrial physical interactions while possessing internal properties that remain independent of the conceptual assumptions underlying those interactions. This condition provides his physiology with a fundamental resistance to abilities that rely upon the target being an ordinary constituent of Earth’s natural biological system, regardless of whether the Sixth Magic is actively reconstructing his surrounding environment.

Absence of the Terrestrial Concept of Death: As a Composite Ultimate One, Avesta does not possess the ordinary terrestrial Concept of Death intrinsic to human life, having acquired a constitution whose biological and existential foundations extend beyond the conditions through which Earth recognizes mortality. In the case of conventional organisms, death represents an irreversible termination of the processes necessary to sustain their existence. Even extraordinary regenerative beings generally retain some relationship between the destruction of their vital functions and the possibility of permanent cessation. Ultimate Ones, however, possess fundamentally different constitutions, and their lack of an applicable terrestrial Concept of Death renders ordinary methods of conceptual killing insufficient. Avesta incorporates this property through the convergence of countless alien ultimate-lifeform characteristics, establishing a condition in which his material body cannot simply be understood as a human organism possessing an exceptionally prolonged lifespan. The destruction of an apparent vital organ does not automatically establish the termination of his complete biological existence, while effects that attempt to actualize an ordinary human endpoint may fail because that endpoint does not correspond to the underlying nature of his composite constitution. This characteristic is separate from the cosmological immortality provided by Replica Universe. Even without considering his independent greater-universal foundation, Avesta possesses a genuine Ultimate One-type absence of ordinary terrestrial death. His greater Universe subsequently provides another layer of existential continuity beyond that condition. Thus, destroying his visible body, overcoming his alien biological immortality, and extinguishing the Replica Universe supporting his complete existence represent distinct accomplishments. Avesta’s lack of terrestrial death does not mean that the logical possibility of his destruction has ceased to exist under every conceivable metaphysical framework, but it does mean that conventional death-based phenomena cannot presume that he possesses the same inherent endpoint as an ordinary human.

Composite Ultimate Physiology — The Convergence of Supreme Lifeforms: Composite Ultimate Physiology is the integrated biological framework through which Avesta expresses the strongest evolutionary characteristics of the innumerable celestial lifeforms assimilated through Retroupdate. Ordinary biological evolution produces organisms whose structures are adapted to particular environments, with their anatomy, metabolism, sensory faculties, and defensive mechanisms developing according to the conditions of their native worlds. Avesta’s physiology is fundamentally different because its constituent traits originate from the culminating evolutionary outcomes of countless such environments rather than the developmental history of a single planet. His body therefore possesses a comprehensive collection of extraordinary biological possibilities, including unconventional methods of energy generation, structural reinforcement, environmental adaptation, regeneration, and interaction with physical phenomena. These characteristics are not necessarily expressed as separate organs visibly attached to an otherwise human body. Through the reconstructed cosmological foundation of Replica Universe, they are incorporated into a unified organism capable of manifesting different configurations according to the demands placed upon its existence. An anatomical function ordinarily performed through a particular biological structure may instead be maintained through an entirely different system inherited from another celestial lifeform. Similarly, his material composition need not remain permanently restricted to conventional organic tissue, because the evolutionary histories incorporated into his constitution may include supreme organisms whose bodies are composed of extraordinary minerals, energetic structures, crystalline substances, or other forms of matter. The composite physiology is consequently an adaptive and internally coordinated system rather than an unstable accumulation of unrelated biological components. Its unity is established through Retroupdate, which reconstructs the developmental conditions supporting the convergence of those traits. Avesta’s body is therefore best understood as a completed artificial supreme species whose physiology contains the cumulative results of innumerable independent evolutionary systems.

Ultimate Cellular Autonomy — Independence of Vital Functions: Ultimate Cellular Autonomy is the condition through which Avesta’s biological functions are distributed throughout his composite organism rather than being exclusively dependent upon a fixed arrangement of vulnerable organs. The most relevant terrestrial comparison is ORT’s extraordinary physiology, in which individual cells possess the functional capabilities of the entire organism and the destruction of conventional vital structures does not automatically terminate its existence. Avesta’s completed composite constitution incorporates analogous self-sustaining biological properties from the supreme lifeforms of Replica Universe, permitting vital functions to be maintained through multiple independent structural configurations. His apparent heart, brain, nervous system, and other recognizable organs may function normally during his human manifestation, but their destruction does not necessarily eliminate the capabilities ordinarily associated with them. The corresponding functions can be maintained through alternative tissues, autonomous cellular structures, or nonstandard biological systems already incorporated into his composite physiology. The consequence is an organism that does not possess the ordinary relationship between anatomical localization and survival. Severing a limb, destroying a particular organ, or inflicting otherwise fatal internal damage cannot be assumed to produce permanent biological cessation. The remaining organism may continue functioning through the distributed capabilities of its constituent structures, while the destroyed components are subsequently reconstructed through its regenerative mechanisms. This property also makes conventional medical knowledge an unreliable basis for identifying a decisive weak point, because the apparent human organization of the body is only one configuration through which Avesta’s composite existence can be expressed. The true significance of Ultimate Cellular Autonomy is that the organism’s biological continuity does not depend upon the survival of any single conventional organ. Its vital functions belong to the composite lifeform as a whole.

Autonomous Restoration — Supreme Cellular Regeneration: Autonomous Restoration is Avesta’s intrinsic regenerative ability, arising from the assimilation of the strongest self-reconstruction mechanisms produced by the celestial lifeforms of Replica Universe. Unlike ordinary regenerative Magecraft, which may require the expenditure of magical energy to reproduce missing tissue or repair damaged structures, this restoration is a natural property of his completed composite organism. Destroyed cells, severed limbs, ruptured organs, and other biological components can be reconstructed through the autonomous processes of his assimilated physiology, permitting recovery from injuries that would cause irreversible death in an ordinary terrestrial organism. Because his internal functions are distributed rather than exclusively dependent upon fixed vital organs, regeneration does not necessarily require the preservation of a conventional anatomical center. The remaining functional structures can continue maintaining the organism while damaged regions are restored. Furthermore, the presence of multiple assimilated regenerative principles allows Avesta’s body to employ different methods of reconstruction according to the nature of the injury. A form of damage that prevents ordinary cellular division may not prevent restoration through another biological or material process incorporated into his constitution. The resulting recovery is therefore not restricted to the limitations of one species’ regenerative system. Nevertheless, Autonomous Restoration must be distinguished from Cosmological Reconstitution, which derives from Avesta’s integration with Replica Universe. Autonomous Restoration operates through his intrinsic Ultimate One physiology, while Cosmological Reconstitution permits the material reexpression of his existence through the greater Universe supporting him. The former makes his living body extraordinarily difficult to destroy; the latter ensures that even the complete loss of a particular manifestation does not necessarily terminate his existence. Together, these mechanisms create an exceptionally comprehensive system of biological and cosmological survival.

Ultimate Evolutionary Adaptation — The Culmination of Countless Histories: Ultimate Evolutionary Adaptation is the ability through which Avesta expresses and combines the supreme developmental characteristics of the lifeforms assimilated from Replica Universe’s reconstructed cosmic histories. Its foundation is the extraordinary evolutionary record produced through one trillion years of Lost History and twelve trillion years of simulated future development, providing the Magician with access to the biological and existential outcomes of countless celestial environments. Rather than relying upon the slow evolutionary processes through which ordinary organisms acquire adaptations across successive generations, Avesta possesses an already established collection of supreme characteristics that can be expressed through his composite physiology. When confronted with an unfamiliar environment or hostile phenomenon, his organism can select and activate the properties most appropriate to its conditions. Extreme temperatures, unusual atmospheric compositions, extraordinary pressures, unfamiliar gravitational fields, corrosive environments, and other physical circumstances may be addressed through the corresponding adaptations developed by the assimilated lifeforms. More unusual threats involving alien matter, abnormal energetic interactions, or unconventional biological interference can likewise be met through properties whose origins lie outside Earth’s evolutionary history. The ability is not limited to selecting one adaptation at a time, because the composite nature of Avesta’s constitution permits multiple compatible characteristics to operate simultaneously. His body can therefore combine defensive, sensory, metabolic, and offensive properties that would ordinarily belong to entirely different species. The Sixth Magic further enhances this adaptability by allowing Retroupdate to reconstruct additional evolutionary possibilities within Replica Universe, establishing new developmental outcomes that may subsequently become part of his physiology. Ultimate Evolutionary Adaptation is consequently the manifestation of an extraordinary biological principle: the strongest characteristics of countless independent evolutionary histories are available to a single organism without requiring that organism to undergo every corresponding developmental sequence personally.

Adaptive Morphogenesis — Reconstruction of the Physical Body: Adaptive Morphogenesis is the ability to alter the physical configuration of Avesta’s body through the controlled expression of the different biological and structural traits incorporated into his composite constitution. His ordinary human appearance is not an illusion concealing a fixed monstrous anatomy, but one of the stable forms through which his integrated organism can manifest. Because his physiology contains the evolutionary characteristics of countless lifeforms, its material arrangement is not permanently restricted to the proportions, skeletal organization, or biological composition of a human body. Avesta may express additional structural reinforcement, specialized sensory organs, crystalline formations, altered musculature, protective surfaces, or other anatomical properties without abandoning the continuity of his individual identity. The more extraordinary manifestations of this ability can produce an armored humanoid form whose dark exterior is reinforced by luminous turquoise structures and enormous asymmetric crystalline appendages extending from the back and limbs. These formations are not merely decorative projections, but material expressions of the alien physiological properties incorporated into his complete existence. Their exact functions may include structural protection, energy circulation, sensory extension, and the manipulation of the unusual physical phenomena associated with his assimilated celestial origins. Adaptive Morphogenesis also permits internal anatomical changes that are not immediately visible from outside the body, allowing Avesta to maintain a human silhouette while employing nonhuman physiological systems beneath its surface. The ability should not be confused with ordinary shapeshifting performed through Magecraft, because the resulting forms are genuine configurations of his composite organism rather than temporary transformations imposed upon an otherwise unchanged body. His physical structure is adaptable because the conditions defining that structure were established through the reconstruction of innumerable celestial evolutionary histories.

Celestial Crystalline Manifestation — The Armored Ultimate Form: Celestial Crystalline Manifestation is a specialized expression of Avesta’s composite physiology in which the alien material and energetic properties inherited from his celestial lifeforms become externally visible as an imposing armored form. His body becomes encased in a dark, angular structure resembling a fusion of organic armor and advanced extraterrestrial machinery, while luminous turquoise nodes emerge across the chest, shoulders, arms, and lower limbs. Enormous crystalline formations extend from his back, possessing irregular violet, pale blue, and crimson structures that resemble wings composed of fractured celestial matter and concentrated energy. These appendages are physical manifestations of the composite organism rather than conventional garments or mechanical equipment, allowing them to participate directly in the circulation and expression of his supernatural abilities. The armor represents an additional biological configuration rather than a simple increase in protective clothing, its durability and functional characteristics arising from the supreme structural properties assimilated from the celestial lifeforms of Replica Universe. The luminous formations may serve as conduits for energy, sensory organs, or the points through which selected alien environmental properties are expressed. His apparent body remains humanoid, but its complete composition is unmistakably foreign to terrestrial biology. This manifestation does not signify that Avesta becomes an entirely separate individual or abandons his ordinary human identity. It is a more extensive expression of the physiology he already possesses, allowing the characteristics of his composite celestial constitution to become materially prominent. The contrast between his reserved human appearance and his armored form reflects the distinction between an individual who continues to behave as a human being and an organism whose underlying biological foundation belongs to countless celestial evolutionary histories.

Composite Celestial Backup — Reinforcement from Countless Celestial Bodies: Composite Celestial Backup is an extraordinary reinforcement mechanism arising from Avesta’s artificial status as the ultimate representative of countless celestial bodies. In TYPE-MOON, Archetype: Earth provides a precedent for an existence receiving direct support from its planetary origin, with the Ultimate One skill allowing the planet to reinforce its representative in response to an opponent. Avesta’s equivalent phenomenon is founded upon a different cosmological structure. Through Retroupdate, the ultimate evolutionary relationships of countless celestial bodies have been established within Replica Universe and concentrated upon his own existence. As a consequence, he possesses an enormous network of celestial connections through which the replica’s astronomical constituents may reinforce the organism representing their collective developmental culmination. This support is not merely an external supply of magical energy, because the relationship concerns the position Avesta occupies within the replica’s cosmological hierarchy. His material manifestation can receive reinforcement through the celestial foundations incorporated into his status, enhancing the physical and supernatural capacities of his composite body. Unlike an ordinary planetary representative whose support originates from one celestial environment, Avesta’s foundation encompasses innumerable bodies whose characteristics and developmental histories have been incorporated into the greater Universe. The reinforcement may therefore reflect multiple celestial properties rather than one planetary system’s ordinary physical conditions. The capacity is especially significant because the celestial bodies providing support are not wholly external entities whose existence must be located through the Actual Universe. Their reconstructed contents are already concentrated within the phase-domain associated with Avesta’s body through Geocentric Retroupdate. Composite Celestial Backup consequently functions as an intrinsic relationship between the Magician and his created cosmos, allowing his ordinary material manifestation to express power derived from the celestial foundations of his own existence without requiring him to separately manifest the entire Replica Universe.

Composite Celestial Authority — The Mandate of Countless Worlds: Composite Celestial Authority is the collective expression of the world-governing faculties inherited or established through the supreme celestial lifeforms assimilated into Avesta’s existence. In TYPE-MOON’s metaphysics, Authority refers to a category of supernatural function that does not merely achieve an outcome through a sequence of thaumaturgical operations, but realizes a phenomenon through the right to govern the corresponding aspect of reality. Although Ultimate Ones do not universally possess identical Divine Authorities, certain celestial representatives and planetary systems demonstrate powers comparable in function to the Authorities of Divine Spirits. Avesta’s case is exceptional because Retroupdate has established him as the ultimate evolutionary representative of countless celestial bodies while integrating their reconstructed cosmological foundations into his own existence. The governing faculties legitimately produced by those celestial histories may consequently be assimilated as part of his composite constitution. These faculties can concern the environmental, material, energetic, biological, or spatial conditions associated with their originating celestial systems, permitting Avesta to exercise authority-like control over phenomena falling within the relevant jurisdictions. The resulting power is not simply a collection of spells copied from unrelated magi, because its foundation is the relationship between the supreme organism and the celestial order whose development produced it. Within Replica Universe, Avesta’s composite status grants him an extraordinary network of genuine celestial jurisdictions, while the Sixth Magic provides the means to reconstruct the larger framework in which those jurisdictions are established. When such an Authority is expressed within the Actual Universe, its operation may depend upon the relevant phase relationship, the manifestation of its corresponding celestial environment, or another means through which the governing system becomes applicable. Composite Celestial Authority does not automatically make Avesta the natural ruler of Earth’s planetary functions or the possessor of every Divine Authority belonging to unrelated gods. Rather, it grants him the extraordinary faculties of the countless celestial systems whose ultimate developmental positions have become his own.

Celestial Environmental Imposition — Composite Alien World Manifestation: Celestial Environmental Imposition is the ability through which Avesta manifests the physical and supernatural conditions associated with the extraterrestrial environments incorporated into his composite constitution. Certain Ultimate Ones demonstrate that their mere presence can impose alien conditions upon a planetary environment, as exemplified by ORT’s Crystal Valley, which overwrites the surrounding physical laws with those corresponding to its own extraterrestrial system. Avesta possesses an analogous but substantially more versatile capacity because his existence does not derive from one alien environment alone. His reconstructed physiology incorporates the characteristics of supreme lifeforms originating from countless celestial bodies, each potentially possessing a different environmental foundation. By expressing those characteristics, Avesta can cause the surrounding region to acquire physical conditions corresponding to a selected celestial origin, producing localized changes in matter, energy, atmospheric properties, and other aspects of the environment. Depending upon the inherited properties being manifested, the resulting region may become dominated by unusual crystalline substances, alien energetic fields, incompatible biological conditions, or other phenomena foreign to terrestrial common sense. Unlike an ordinary Reality Marble, this ability is not necessarily the projection of Avesta’s personal mental landscape. It is a manifestation of the environmental characteristics naturally associated with the celestial lifeforms incorporated into his existence. The Sixth Magic further amplifies its scope by permitting corresponding regions of Replica Universe to become materially expressed through Phase Materialization. Avesta may therefore impose an alien environment through his intrinsic Ultimate One physiology while simultaneously drawing upon the independently existing cosmic structures supporting that environment. The resulting phenomenon combines a native extraterrestrial environmental faculty with the capacity to reproduce its underlying astronomical conditions through True Magic, creating an interaction between biological world-imposition and cosmological reconstruction.

Planetary Phenomenon Regulation — Authority over Celestial Conditions: Planetary Phenomenon Regulation is the capacity to govern selected environmental and physical processes through the authority-like functions associated with Avesta’s assimilated celestial origins. In the case of a natural planetary Archetype, the organism may possess direct access to the planet’s functions, allowing it to influence environmental systems through a relationship fundamentally different from conventional Magecraft. Avesta’s artificial composite status creates a comparable possibility across the countless celestial systems represented within Replica Universe. The relevant functions may encompass atmospheric circulation, material transformation, gravitational relationships, energetic interactions, environmental stabilization, and other conditions through which a celestial body maintains its internal order. These operations are not necessarily performed through the calculation of innumerable independent physical interactions. Where the corresponding Authority has been legitimately established within the replica’s reconstructed history, Avesta may exercise the associated function through his position as the supreme representative of that celestial system. The ability is particularly effective when employed alongside Retroupdate, which can alter the comprehensive cosmological model supporting those conditions. However, the two mechanisms remain distinct. Planetary Phenomenon Regulation expresses the faculties of Avesta’s composite celestial constitution, whereas Retroupdate reconstructs the Universe in which those faculties operate. The combination allows Avesta to regulate individual environmental systems through his inherited Authorities while employing the Sixth Magic to remodel their larger astronomical relationships. The resulting capacity is not simply elemental manipulation performed on an enormous scale. It represents the operation of celestial functions through the authority of a being whose existence has been made the cumulative ultimate lifeform of the corresponding worlds.

Celestial Energy Circulation — The Breath of Countless Worlds: Celestial Energy Circulation is the extraordinary energetic function through which Avesta’s composite organism processes, converts, and expresses the diverse forms of energy associated with his assimilated celestial lifeforms. Certain planetary beings in TYPE-MOON possess functions analogous to the breathing of a planet, absorbing external magical energy and returning it to the environment through their own internal circulation. Other Ultimate Ones possess fundamentally different energetic constitutions, including organisms whose bodies are composed of extraordinary forms of matter or whose internal structures resemble stellar mechanisms. Avesta’s physiology incorporates the supreme energetic characteristics produced by countless celestial environments, allowing his body to sustain multiple forms of energy circulation through an integrated biological framework. His luminous turquoise structures may function as visible expressions of this internal circulation, distributing energy throughout the organism and supporting the activation of its extraordinary physiological capabilities. The ability is not restricted to conventional human magical energy, because the contributing lifeforms may have developed under physical conditions incompatible with ordinary terrestrial metabolism. Consequently, Avesta may possess access to energetic mechanisms involving unusual radiation, alien matter interactions, or other forms of physical and supernatural energy established through Replica Universe. The circulation of these energies can reinforce his material body, sustain the manifestation of specialized biological configurations, and support the operation of his environmental faculties. Because the celestial systems contributing to his constitution are integrated into the greater Replica Universe, the Magician also possesses an extraordinary foundation through which their corresponding energetic properties can remain available. Celestial Energy Circulation therefore represents the metabolic aspect of his composite supremacy: a single organism capable of expressing the energetic functions of innumerable supreme lifeforms through a unified physical and cosmological constitution.

Extraterrestrial Structural Supremacy — Alien Physical Characteristics: Extraterrestrial Structural Supremacy is the collective enhancement of Avesta’s physical capabilities through the assimilation of the strongest structural and biomechanical characteristics developed by the lifeforms of Replica Universe. Ultimate Ones are not restricted to the ordinary physical limits of terrestrial organisms, and their material constitutions may display combinations of properties that would be incompatible with familiar biological structures. ORT, for example, possesses an extraordinary outer surface whose resistance, flexibility, thermal tolerance, and sharpness exceed conventional terrestrial expectations. Avesta’s composite organism incorporates analogous supreme characteristics from countless celestial environments, granting his material body an extensive collection of exceptional structural properties. His physical surfaces may possess extraordinary resistance to mechanical destruction, while his internal structures can adopt configurations appropriate to different environmental pressures and energetic conditions. The organism’s composition may also exhibit properties inherited from lifeforms whose physical structures do not resemble conventional organic matter, including crystalline, metallic, energetic, or otherwise exotic forms of biological organization. These characteristics permit his manifested body to function under conditions that would annihilate ordinary lifeforms long before the Sixth Magic’s cosmological protection became relevant. His strength, movement, physical endurance, and capacity to deliver destructive force are therefore supported by genuine extraterrestrial physiology, not merely by the fact that a greater Universe exists within him. Nevertheless, the complete magnitude of any particular physical action depends upon the characteristics being expressed, and the creation of Replica Universe does not require every ordinary movement to release universe-destroying force. His physical supremacy arises from the collective evolutionary characteristics of the strongest celestial lifeforms, while his greatest cosmological feats remain applications of the Sixth True Magic.

Extraterrestrial Sensory Integration — Perception Beyond Human Biology: Extraterrestrial Sensory Integration is the ability through which Avesta perceives his surroundings using the extraordinary sensory mechanisms inherited from the supreme lifeforms of countless celestial bodies. Human perception is limited by biological organs adapted to the conditions of Earth, relying upon a relatively narrow range of electromagnetic radiation, mechanical vibration, and chemical interaction. The lifeforms of Replica Universe, however, may have evolved under vastly different physical conditions, producing sensory systems capable of detecting phenomena that terrestrial organisms would not naturally recognize. Through the assimilation of those characteristics, Avesta possesses a composite perceptual framework capable of incorporating multiple forms of environmental information simultaneously. Depending upon the sensory faculties being expressed, his perception may extend to unusual energetic disturbances, changes in material composition, spatial abnormalities, biological activity, and other physical relationships relevant to the celestial environments from which those faculties originated. These sensory systems do not necessarily require recognizable human eyes, ears, or other ordinary organs, because the information may be processed through distributed biological structures or specialized components of his alien physiology. His luminous crystalline formations and armored appendages may consequently serve as sensory interfaces in addition to their structural and energetic functions. The Sixth Magic further expands the usefulness of these faculties by permitting the material expression of environmental conditions belonging to Replica Universe, allowing the Magician to perceive phenomena through sensory systems specifically adapted to those conditions. Nevertheless, possessing an immense range of sensory capabilities does not automatically grant omniscience or unrestricted knowledge of the Swirl of the Root. The ability concerns perception through extraordinarily advanced and diverse biological mechanisms, not the automatic possession of every fact concerning existence.

Celestial Predation and Conceptual Assimilation: Celestial Predation and Conceptual Assimilation are abilities through which Avesta expresses the absorptive and adaptive characteristics of predatory supreme lifeforms incorporated into his composite physiology. TYPE-MOON provides a relevant precedent in Type Venus, an extraordinary parasitic Ultimate One capable of extending itself through numerous predatory terminals and absorbing concepts associated with the beings it encounters. Avesta’s assimilation of the ultimate evolutionary outcomes of countless celestial bodies permits the incorporation of comparable faculties, allowing his organism to acquire biological information, material characteristics, and certain conceptual properties through appropriate forms of interaction. This does not require him to consume every target through conventional biological digestion, as the specific process may depend upon the absorptive mechanisms inherited from the relevant celestial lifeforms. A material organism might be analyzed through direct biological contact, while a more unusual existence could require a predatory mechanism capable of interacting with its spiritual, informational, or conceptual constitution. The information acquired through such encounters may subsequently be incorporated into Avesta’s adaptive physiology, providing additional characteristics for his composite organism to express. The Sixth Magic offers a further possibility by allowing these newly acquired properties to be examined through Retroupdate and incorporated into the reconstructed evolutionary histories of Replica Universe. Celestial Predation therefore operates as a native capacity for biological and conceptual acquisition, while Retroupdate provides a means of integrating the results into a much greater cosmological framework. The ability should not be confused with an automatic power to claim every supernatural Authority through contact alone. Its function depends upon the nature of the predatory mechanism and the relationship between the organism and the property being assimilated. Nevertheless, as a composite of countless supreme lifeforms, Avesta possesses an extraordinarily extensive foundation of absorptive and adaptive mechanisms unavailable to an ordinary human magus.

Autonomous Terminal Generation — Extensions of the Composite Organism: Autonomous Terminal Generation is the ability through which Avesta can express distributed biological structures or independent extensions of his composite organism, drawing upon the reproductive and proliferative properties of the supreme celestial lifeforms whose characteristics he possesses. Certain Ultimate Ones demonstrate extraordinary methods of extending their influence through numerous subsidiary organisms, as exemplified by Type Venus and its immense collection of predatory terminals. Avesta’s corresponding faculty allows portions of his composite physiology to be expressed as autonomous or semi-autonomous structures possessing selected characteristics of the greater organism. These terminals need not reproduce his entire cosmological foundation or function as independently complete Sixth Magicians. Instead, they may serve as extensions capable of observation, environmental interaction, biological acquisition, or the manifestation of particular alien physiological properties. Their forms can reflect the diverse evolutionary systems incorporated into Avesta’s constitution, permitting the production of organisms or structures adapted to specialized purposes. Because his composite existence is maintained through a unified cosmological identity, the terminals may remain connected to the principal organism through biological, informational, or phase-based relationships, allowing their observations and acquired information to contribute to his broader understanding. The Sixth Magic may further facilitate their deployment by permitting selected structures belonging to Replica Universe to undergo Phase Materialization. This combination gives Avesta the ability to distribute aspects of his biological existence across an environment without requiring his principal material body to occupy every relevant location. The terminals remain expressions of his composite physiology rather than automatically independent Ultimate Ones, and their destruction does not necessarily compromise the complete organism. Autonomous Terminal Generation consequently provides an additional means of reconnaissance, environmental adaptation, and distributed biological activity, supplementing the Magician’s more comprehensive cosmological operations.

Celestial Ecological Genesis — Creation and Cultivation of Alien Life: Celestial Ecological Genesis is an authority-like function associated with the life-generating histories incorporated into Avesta’s composite existence. Through Retroupdate, he unlawfully reproduced Earth’s potential to create Life across the celestial bodies of Replica Universe, establishing the conditions through which those environments could develop their own evolutionary systems and ultimate representatives. Following his transformation into the Composite Ultimate One, the resulting biological and ecological characteristics became part of the framework supporting his existence. Avesta can therefore express the life-generating and ecosystem-forming faculties legitimately incorporated through those histories, allowing him to influence the development of alien biological environments within the jurisdictions established by his created cosmos. This capacity differs from simply producing organisms through ordinary biological engineering, because its foundation concerns the relationship between a celestial environment and the potential for life to emerge within it. Through his composite Authorities, Avesta may cultivate ecological conditions appropriate to particular assimilated lifeforms, establish suitable environments for their development, or initiate forms of biological proliferation associated with his supreme celestial constitution. In conjunction with Phase Materialization, selected environments and organisms originating from Replica Universe can potentially be expressed within the Actual Universe, although their interaction with terrestrial reality remains subject to the phase relationship through which they manifest. The power does not make Avesta the natural source of every lifeform throughout all possible realities, nor does it grant him ownership over every living organism on Earth. Its authority is established through the cosmological histories of Replica Universe and the celestial systems whose ultimate life-generating functions have been assimilated into his own existence. Celestial Ecological Genesis consequently represents the constructive counterpart to his destructive abilities, allowing him to cultivate the conditions of living worlds rather than merely exercise supremacy over their inhabitants.

Composite Celestial Communication — Communion with Astronomical Origins: Composite Celestial Communication is the ability through which Avesta maintains relationships with the celestial foundations incorporated into his Composite Ultimate One status. In TYPE-MOON, certain Ultimate Ones possess a direct connection to their planets of origin, and Type Saturn demonstrates the capacity to receive and relay the commands of celestial bodies. Avesta’s completed composite existence possesses an artificial equivalent of this relationship on an extraordinary scale. Through Retroupdate, the developmental histories and ultimate representative positions of countless celestial bodies have been integrated into the central cosmological structure associated with his body. These relationships permit the Magician to receive and interpret information associated with the conditions, functions, and developments of the celestial systems represented within Replica Universe. Such communication should not be understood exclusively as verbal conversation between the Magician and countless independent human-like planetary minds. Celestial bodies may not possess consciousness in a form recognizable to terrestrial organisms, and their relationship with an Ultimate One need not resemble ordinary dialogue. Instead, the connection may involve the transmission of environmental information, cosmological conditions, or other forms of planetary recognition through the existential framework linking Avesta to the corresponding celestial histories. The Sixth Magic provides the larger structure through which these relationships remain coordinated, while his composite Ultimate One physiology allows the resulting information to be expressed through a unified individual consciousness. This makes Avesta more than a lifeform possessing borrowed planetary traits. Within Replica Universe, he occupies a position through which the supreme developmental relationships of innumerable celestial bodies converge, allowing their associated information and functions to become part of his own operational existence.

Composite Evolutionary Archive — The Knowledge of Supreme Species: Composite Evolutionary Archive is the vast biological and developmental information contained within Avesta’s completed Ultimate One constitution, representing the accumulated outcomes of one trillion years of reconstructed Lost History and twelve trillion years of simulated future development. Each assimilated celestial lifeform contributes information concerning the environmental conditions, adaptations, physical characteristics, and developmental processes through which it attained the position of the strongest existence associated with its celestial origin. The resulting collection constitutes an extraordinary archive of evolutionary possibilities, including biological systems that may never have arisen within the Actual Universe. Unlike ordinary scientific knowledge acquired through study, this information is incorporated into the very constitution of Avesta’s organism, permitting relevant characteristics to be expressed through his physiology without requiring the corresponding evolutionary sequence to be repeated. The archive also supplies the foundation for Ultimate Evolutionary Adaptation, allowing the organism to select from the enormous collection of established traits when responding to unfamiliar circumstances. Through the Sixth Magic, additional developmental histories may be reconstructed and integrated into the archive, permitting the possible expansion of its contents beyond those established during the original thirteen-trillion-year transformation. Nevertheless, the existence of this archive does not require Avesta’s conscious mind to possess immediate, complete understanding of every event or phenomenon represented within it. Its significance lies in the objective accumulation of evolutionary information and the biological access his composite constitution possesses to the resulting characteristics. The archive therefore functions as both an extraordinary repository of cosmic biological development and the informational foundation supporting the adaptive versatility of the Composite Ultimate One.

Composite Cosmic Resistance — Layered Existential Defenses: Composite Cosmic Resistance is the collective defensive condition arising from the combination of Avesta’s alien Ultimate One constitution, autonomous biological restoration, celestial reinforcement, and independent cosmological foundation. Each of these properties addresses a different category of threat, preventing his survival from depending upon a single form of protection. His alien constitution invalidates assumptions concerning ordinary terrestrial damage and mortality, while Ultimate Cellular Autonomy allows biological functions to continue despite the destruction of conventional vital structures. Autonomous Restoration provides the capacity to reconstruct damaged components through the regenerative mechanisms inherited from his assimilated lifeforms, and Ultimate Evolutionary Adaptation permits his body to express additional characteristics suited to unfamiliar forms of attack. Composite Celestial Backup subsequently reinforces his manifested organism through the celestial foundations whose ultimate evolutionary positions he occupies. Beyond these physiological defenses lies the greater protection of Universal Existential Integration, through which his continued existence is supported by Replica Universe. Consequently, even if an opponent possesses a phenomenon capable of overcoming one aspect of his alien constitution, that accomplishment does not automatically defeat the remaining systems. An attack capable of destroying ordinary cells may fail to terminate his distributed biological functions, while a phenomenon capable of eliminating the entire material manifestation may still leave the greater Universe supporting his existence intact. The resulting defenses are not merely multiple layers of conventional armor, but distinct biological, conceptual, and cosmological mechanisms established through the convergence of countless celestial lifeforms and the Sixth Magic. This makes Avesta’s complete elimination extraordinarily difficult, requiring an opponent to overcome not only his native Ultimate One physiology but also the independent greater-universal foundation from which his material existence can be restored.

Celestial Combat Adaptation — Expression of the Supreme Lifeforms: Celestial Combat Adaptation is the ability through which Avesta employs the physical and supernatural characteristics of his composite constitution in response to the particular demands of combat. Rather than possessing only a fixed collection of offensive techniques, his organism contains the supreme developmental properties of countless lifeforms whose evolutionary histories may have produced radically different methods of attack, defense, movement, and environmental control. Avesta can therefore select and combine the relevant characteristics according to the nature of an opponent, employing extraordinary structural reinforcement against physical attacks, alien sensory systems against concealed threats, specialized energetic mechanisms against hostile environments, or appropriate environmental properties when confronting beings whose defenses depend upon particular physical conditions. The versatility of this ability derives from the completeness of his reconstructed evolutionary foundation rather than from an unrestricted power to invent any desired result. Because the corresponding characteristics already belong to his completed composite constitution, their expression constitutes the activation of legitimate biological capabilities rather than the acquisition of unrelated supernatural techniques through imitation alone. When combined with Composite Celestial Authority, the same process may involve the expression of appropriate environmental or world-governing faculties associated with the contributing celestial histories. Retroupdate further expands the strategic possibilities by permitting the reconstruction of additional developmental outcomes within Replica Universe. The resulting combat style is exceptionally adaptable, although its exact expression remains influenced by Avesta’s own judgment, knowledge, and deliberate selection of appropriate capabilities. His immense physiological versatility complements his established personality as a patient, analytical, and pragmatic individual who prefers the efficient application of power to unnecessary displays of force.

Ultimate One Extermination Potential — The Supreme Celestial Organism: Ultimate One Extermination Potential is the capacity for overwhelming destructive and ecological dominance inherent in Avesta’s status as the composite culmination of countless supreme celestial lifeforms. In TYPE-MOON’s Notes., individual Aristoteles are described as beings possessing sufficient power to exterminate the remaining lifeforms of Earth, with their extraordinary physical and environmental characteristics making conventional terrestrial defenses inadequate. Avesta’s completed constitution incorporates the supreme biological and supernatural properties of innumerable celestial origins, producing an organism whose potential for environmental domination and large-scale destruction extends far beyond that of a conventional terrestrial lifeform. Through his native physiological capabilities, he can express extraordinary material strength, energetic phenomena, biological proliferation, and alien environmental conditions, while his Composite Celestial Authorities permit the operation of functions associated with the celestial systems whose supreme representative he has become. His Sixth Magic provides an additional and fundamentally distinct means of affecting astronomical structures and cosmological relationships, allowing Retroupdate and Phase Materialization to operate beyond the ordinary capacities of his material body. The interaction between these systems makes Avesta exceptionally dangerous, although his existence as a Composite Ultimate One does not automatically compel him to exterminate other lifeforms or behave according to the instincts of every species whose characteristics he has inherited. His individual identity and personality remain intact, allowing him to determine whether and how these powers are exercised. Ultimate One Extermination Potential therefore describes the extraordinary capacities inherent in his completed constitution rather than an unavoidable behavioral imperative. The Sixth Magician possesses an organism capable of expressing the supreme destructive and environmental characteristics of countless celestial lifeforms, but their deployment remains subject to his conscious decisions.

Celestial Authority Synchronization — Unity of the Composite Whole: Celestial Authority Synchronization is the principle through which the numerous biological, supernatural, and authority-like faculties incorporated into Avesta’s existence are maintained as components of a single functional organism. Ordinarily, the supreme lifeforms of different celestial bodies would possess independent constitutions, with their abilities developing under environmental conditions and cosmological relationships that might be mutually incompatible. The convergence of such lifeforms into one body would therefore present extraordinary problems of biological integration and metaphysical coherence. Avesta circumvents these difficulties through Retroupdate, which reconstructs the historical foundation of Replica Universe so that the assimilated evolutionary characteristics belong to a unified cosmological existence. Their coexistence is not merely enforced through continuous suppression of incompatible traits. Rather, the completed composite organism possesses an internally valid developmental foundation in which those properties have become legitimate constituents of its nature. As a consequence, Avesta can coordinate different physiological mechanisms and celestial Authorities without requiring every contributing species to retain an independent body or consciousness. The operation of one capability may support another, allowing energy circulation to reinforce environmental imposition, adaptive morphology to express specialized offensive structures, and celestial backup to sustain the physical manifestation of extraordinary biological configurations. The Sixth Magic’s greater cosmological framework provides the foundation through which these relationships remain established, while the Composite Ultimate One constitution embodies their completed biological convergence. Celestial Authority Synchronization therefore makes Avesta something fundamentally different from a collection of unrelated extraterrestrial organisms. He is a single ultimate lifeform whose abilities originate from countless celestial histories but have been integrated into one coherent existence.

Universal-Celestial Symbiosis — The Union of True Magic and Ultimate One: Universal-Celestial Symbiosis is the completed relationship between Avesta’s Sixth True Magic and his artificial Composite Ultimate One physiology, through which the abilities of the two systems reinforce one another without becoming identical in their underlying principles. Replica Universe provides the independent cosmological framework, fourteenth-dimensional Overlay, Phase Materialization, and Retroupdate necessary to create and reconstruct a Universe perpetually greater than the Actual Universe. The Composite Ultimate One constitution provides the extraordinary physical, biological, sensory, regenerative, adaptive, and celestial authority-like faculties derived from the supreme evolutionary lifeforms of that created cosmos. These two foundations are inseparably connected because the same reconstructed celestial histories that establish Avesta’s status as an Ultimate One also belong to the Universe whose contents have been internalized within his body. His material organism may therefore employ the extraordinary characteristics of its assimilated lifeforms while receiving support from the celestial structures associated with those characteristics. Similarly, his Sixth Magic may reconstruct the environments or histories supporting a particular ability, permitting its underlying conditions to be modified through Retroupdate. The combination creates a relationship in which Avesta’s body is both the supreme composite organism of Replica Universe and the central location of its reconstructed celestial totality. However, the distinction between the two remains significant. His intrinsic Ultimate One physiology does not cease to possess its alien biological characteristics merely because he is not actively performing a Universe Update, while the Sixth Magic’s complete cosmological abilities are not reducible to ordinary functions of his biological tissues. Universal-Celestial Symbiosis is therefore the culmination of two extraordinary achievements: the creation of a greater Universe through True Magic and the artificial establishment of its countless supreme celestial lifeforms within the constitution of their creator.

The Artificial Aristoteles of Countless Worlds: Avesta Lorsing Manich’s Composite Ultimate One abilities establish him as an extraordinary artificial celestial existence whose nature differs fundamentally from that of a conventional Magician, a naturally occurring Ultimate One, or a Divine Spirit exercising Authority over a particular aspect of the World. His completed constitution encompasses the extraterrestrial common-sense independence, absence of ordinary terrestrial death, autonomous biological restoration, extraordinary structural characteristics, adaptive physiology, and environmental faculties associated with the supreme lifeforms of countless celestial origins. Through Retroupdate, these characteristics have been incorporated into a single organism whose developmental foundation extends across one trillion years of reconstructed Lost History and twelve trillion years of simulated future evolution. The resulting Composite Celestial Authority permits the expression of the governing faculties established through those histories, while Composite Celestial Backup reinforces the organism through the celestial bodies whose ultimate positions he occupies. His ability to adapt, reconstruct, and express different biological and environmental systems gives him a degree of physical and supernatural versatility fundamentally distinct from the properties of any individual naturally occurring TYPE. Nevertheless, the most significant characteristic of Avesta’s existence is the complete integration of this composite physiology with Replica Universe. His alien organism is not supported solely by its biological integrity, nor is his continued existence restricted to the survival of one planetary environment. The greater Universe he created serves as the foundation through which his composite constitution, reconstructed history, and material manifestation remain established. Consequently, the destruction of his physical body cannot automatically be equated with his complete elimination, while the extraordinary biological properties of his Ultimate One status ensure that even reaching the point of total material destruction presents a formidable challenge. His offensive faculties are similarly extensive, allowing him to employ the supreme physical characteristics, alien environmental phenomena, biological assimilation mechanisms, and authority-like functions of countless celestial lifeforms before considering the more comprehensive cosmological operations of Retroupdate or the terminal conceptual effects of All-Hanging Heat Death — Orbertall. These capabilities do not make him identical to Akasha or the natural sovereign of every celestial body in the Actual Universe, but they establish his genuine supremacy within the reconstructed evolutionary order of Replica Universe. His existence represents the convergence of innumerable planetary possibilities into a single individual, an artificial Aristoteles whose biological constitution has become as extraordinary as the cosmological framework sustaining it. Where an ordinary Ultimate One is the supreme existence of a celestial origin, Avesta is the cumulative supreme existence of countless celestial origins whose histories were reconstructed to converge upon him. The Sixth Magic created the greater Universe, Retroupdate established its celestial history, and the Composite Ultimate One transformation made Avesta Lorsing Manich the ultimate living expression of that Universe’s innumerable evolutionary conclusions.

MYSTIC CODE
All-Hanging Heat Death — Orbertall (万象終焉・オルベルタル, Banshō Shūen: Oruberutaru) is a supreme conceptual armament and specialized Mystic Code created by the Sixth Magician through the application of the Sixth True Magic, Replica Universe, possessing the extraordinary ability to weaponize the eventual thermodynamic ending of the Universe as a means of eliminating any existence contained within its cosmological framework, regardless of whether that existence possesses a personal Concept of Death. Although its appearance resembles an enormous, intricately constructed crimson rifle, with a disproportionately elongated barrel, angular mechanical components, luminous scarlet circuitry, and an immense circular mechanism resembling a cosmological observation apparatus, the weapon does not operate according to the conventional principles of firearms, magical artillery, or even the ordinary conceptual armaments employed by magi. Its true function is the identification, isolation, and premature actualization of an infinitesimal subsection of the Universe’s eventual heat death, permitting the Sixth Magician to impose the terminal condition of the greater cosmos upon a designated existence without requiring the remainder of the Universe to experience that ending. In the terminology of the Mage’s Association, Orbertall would be classified as a Mystic Code possessing an independently established Limited Function, although the phenomenon it executes cannot be reproduced through conventional Magecraft. This classification is particularly significant because Mystic Codes are not restricted to storing magical energy or supporting thaumaturgical formulas; sufficiently extraordinary examples can reproduce specialized applications of a Magician’s True Magic, as demonstrated by the Jeweled Sword Zelretch, which operates upon the Second Magic without conferring the complete authority of the Second Magician upon its wielder. Orbertall follows a corresponding principle, functioning as a specialized armament through which a designated application of Replica Universe is expressed in the form of a firearm. Nevertheless, its operation remains dependent upon the Sixth Magic’s fundamental capacity to actualize an independently existing cosmological framework and reconstruct the historical and causal conditions governing that framework through Retroupdate. It is therefore not a conventional weapon whose destructive capacity derives from its physical construction, but a mechanism through which the Sixth Magician translates a cosmological impossibility into an executable offensive phenomenon. The fundamental principle embodied by Orbertall arises from the distinction between the death of an individual existence and the eventual ending of the Universe containing that existence. Ordinarily, the termination of a living organism is determined through conditions intrinsic to the organism itself, including biological mortality, spiritual continuity, and the metaphysical relationship between an existence and its Concept of Death. The Mystic Eyes of Death Perception represent one of the most extraordinary manifestations of this principle, allowing their possessor to perceive the death belonging to an existence as lines or points and actualize that death through an appropriate physical action. Such phenomena are not merely methods of inflicting conventional injuries, because the destruction produced by the Mystic Eyes is understood as a consequence of an ending that has already been actualized rather than an injury that subsequently causes death. Nevertheless, their operation remains fundamentally concerned with the death or existential limit belonging to the target itself. An existence that possesses no applicable Concept of Death presents an entirely different problem, because the necessary endpoint may be absent from its constitution. Ultimate Ones such as ORT exemplify this difficulty, possessing alien biological and existential structures that do not conform to the ordinary conditions of terrestrial mortality. Orbertall does not attempt to overcome this obstacle by locating an invisible weakness within such beings, nor does it require the Sixth Magician to acquire a superior form of the Mystic Eyes of Death Perception. Instead, it disregards the question of whether the target possesses a death of its own and directs its operation toward the greater cosmological framework in which the target exists. In this respect, the rifle’s conceptual foundation is more closely related to the distinction between an individual existence and the World sustaining that existence. A being may be genuinely immortal according to the principles of its own constitution while nevertheless remaining contained within a greater system whose continuation is not guaranteed by the individual’s immortality. The distinction is especially important because an immortal organism’s inability to die does not automatically establish that every surrounding physical law, region of spacetime, celestial structure, or cosmological framework must continue existing indefinitely for its benefit. Even when an individual existence possesses no natural terminal point, the greater Universe containing that existence may possess a terminal condition of its own. Orbertall weaponizes precisely this discrepancy. Rather than declaring that the target’s individual lifespan has reached its conclusion, the weapon establishes that the portion of the Universe containing the target has already undergone the terminal condition belonging to the greater cosmological whole. In ordinary cosmological models, the eventual heat death of the Universe describes a state in which the expansion and thermodynamic development of the cosmos lead toward the exhaustion of usable energy gradients and the cessation of processes capable of sustaining complex physical activity. This is not, by itself, a scientifically established process through which spacetime is erased or every object instantaneously vanishes, and the ultimate physical fate of the Universe is not known with absolute certainty. Orbertall’s phenomenon must therefore be distinguished from an ordinary acceleration of thermodynamic entropy. Through Replica Universe, the Sixth Magician establishes a determinate cosmological model whose terminal condition corresponds to universal heat death, using Retroupdate to treat that future ending as an actualizable condition rather than merely a prediction concerning distant physical processes. Once the terminal state has been established within the model, the Magic identifies the infinitesimal portion of that ending corresponding to the intended target’s existence and imposes it upon the present through a retroactive Universe Update. The weapon does not accelerate every particle within the target until an immense amount of entropy has accumulated, nor does it require the entire astronomical history preceding heat death to unfold within the span of an ordinary instant. Instead, it skips the causal progression that would ordinarily separate the present from the Universe’s terminal condition and actualizes the selected result directly. The target is consequently subjected not to the physical process of universal heat death, but to the Sixth Magic’s reconstruction of what it means for the designated portion of the Universe to have already reached that ending. This is the fundamental impossibility embodied by Orbertall: the death of the Universe is brought forward only for the portion corresponding to a selected existence, while every surrounding subsection continues along its ordinary cosmological history. The distinction is so extreme that it cannot be adequately understood as accelerated time, entropy manipulation, thermal destruction, or even ordinary reality erasure. It is the premature establishment of a terminal cosmological fact through the isolation of a particular subsection of universal existence. Retroupdate functions as the mechanism through which this contradiction becomes possible, because Replica Universe possesses an independent cosmological framework capable of reconstructing the relationships between space, time, matter, energy, and the historical conditions supporting their existence. The Sixth Magician employs this greater framework as a reference through which the eventual ending of the targeted Universe can be modeled and its corresponding subsection identified without imposing that ending upon the entire cosmic totality. The process resembles the extraction of a single conclusion from an otherwise immeasurably extensive history, except that the conclusion is not merely observed or recorded but forcibly actualized in the present. The original Universe does not need to undergo its complete thermodynamic development, and the target does not need to survive until the remote age at which the terminal condition would ordinarily emerge. The selected ending is made to occur independently of its preceding causes. This also differentiates Orbertall from the Fifth Magic’s demonstrated displacement of time, because the rifle does not simply transport the target into the distant future or transfer the interval containing its death elsewhere. Likewise, it does not require the Second Magic to retrieve a destroyed version of the target from an existing parallel world. The relevant terminal result is established through a direct application of the Sixth Magic’s own reconstructive principle. Although TYPE-MOON’s cosmology recognizes Quantum Time-Locks as mechanisms that preserve particular historical outcomes against ordinary alterations of the past, Orbertall’s operation does not depend upon rewriting such a fixed historical event. It produces a localized terminal condition in the present through an independent cosmological operation, rather than requiring the chronological past of Proper Human History to be modified so that the target was always dead. Nor should its mechanism be confused with Goetia’s Human Order Incineration, through which the accumulated history of humanity was converted into an immense quantity of heat and magical energy for the purpose of reaching a primordial point in planetary history. Orbertall does not harvest the heat of historical events as fuel, and the magnitude of its effect is not determined by converting a fixed number of years into a corresponding quantity of destructive energy. Its operation is instead based upon the actualization of a terminal state whose causal prerequisites have been bypassed through True Magic. As a consequence, the weapon violates the ordinary physical expectations governing conservation and causal succession, not because it simply produces an impossible quantity of thermal energy, but because the result of a cosmic process is established without reproducing the transformations that would ordinarily account for that result. The conceptual classification of the weapon is therefore closer to a cosmological execution apparatus than a conventional firearm, and its apparent projectile should be understood as the medium through which the fixed terminal condition is applied rather than as the source of the destructive effect itself. The most important preparatory operation is the identification of the target’s universal subsection, a process through which the Sixth Magic determines the exact relationship between a designated existence and the greater cosmic framework containing it. Every being, object, phenomenon, and region of space belonging to a Universe constitutes some portion of that Universe’s total existence, regardless of how insignificant that portion may appear when compared with the complete cosmos. A human organism occupies an infinitesimal position within the universe’s material and historical structure, but an Ultimate One, a spiritual existence, or a being possessing a fundamentally alien constitution is likewise included within a greater cosmological framework whenever its existence genuinely resides there. Orbertall does not evaluate these subjects according to a hierarchy of personal lifespans or the strength of their resistance to ordinary death. Instead, it identifies the subsection of the Universe’s total terminal condition corresponding to their participation in that framework. The distinction can be expressed through the analogy of an immense canvas representing the Universe, upon which every individual existence appears as a small mark or stain. The destruction of the mark through conventional means would leave the canvas intact, just as the death of an organism ordinarily leaves the surrounding space and its physical laws undisturbed. Orbertall does something fundamentally different. It identifies the portion of the canvas’s eventual destruction corresponding to the selected mark and actualizes the destruction of that particular portion prematurely. The mark is thereby eliminated, but the small section of canvas upon which it existed is also removed. The surrounding canvas remains intact, even though one infinitesimal subsection has already experienced the ending that properly belongs to the entire canvas in its final state. This analogy captures the true nature of the weapon’s ability more accurately than descriptions involving immense temperatures or explosive force. Orbertall does not merely burn the target away; it eliminates the corresponding portion of the universal framework through which the target’s existence was established. The effect is not necessarily restricted to the apparent size of a physical body, because the relevant subsection is determined by the target’s cosmological relationship rather than its visible anatomical dimensions. An existence distributed across multiple physical manifestations, spiritual vessels, or informational structures may possess a more complicated universal subsection than a conventional organism. The Sixth Magic must identify that subsection as the intended target before the corresponding terminal condition can be fixed. This is the reason the weapon’s capacity to affect unusual modes of existence is not dependent upon whether those modes possess conventional matter. An informational entity may lack a physical body, but the information composing or expressing its existence still occupies a relationship with the Universe in which it is realized. A digital being may possess no biological lifespan, but its informational actuality is nevertheless supported by a cosmological system. A spiritual or equivocal existence may lack stable material anatomy while retaining a determinate connection to the World containing it. Even an existence described as nonexistent in its own right may be subject to Orbertall if that description refers to a paradoxical, virtual, or otherwise unconventional condition whose actuality is still included within the universal framework. In such cases, the weapon does not need to grant the target ordinary physical existence or create a personal Concept of Death before the attack can function. It requires only that the target possess a cosmological subsection that can be designated through Replica Universe. Absolute nonexistence possessing no relationship with any applicable cosmological framework would provide no subsection to identify, but an entity whose apparent nonexistence is merely an unusual mode of participation within the Universe remains eligible for designation. Once the relevant subsection has been determined, the Sixth Magic manifests the Immutable Red Spiral, a luminous crimson formation resembling an irregular fracture or spiral-shaped crack upon the target’s ontological existence. The spiral is not a natural Line of Death, nor is it a pre-existing Point of Death waiting to be perceived through extraordinary Mystic Eyes. It is an artificial designation produced by the Sixth Magic to identify the precise subsection of the Universe whose eventual ending has been selected for premature actualization. Its appearance may resemble a wound in the target’s body, a scarlet fissure suspended upon an immaterial manifestation, or a crack spreading through the spatial region corresponding to an otherwise intangible existence, but its actual significance is independent of those visible forms. The mark represents the point of correspondence between an existence in the continuing present and the terminal condition of the greater Universe containing it. It is described as Immutable because the designated relationship is fixed through Retroupdate once the targeting operation has been successfully completed. Ordinary healing, regeneration, changes in biological condition, or resistance to conceptual mortality do not transform the designation into an ordinary injury that can simply be repaired. The target has not yet been killed, and the presence of the spiral does not automatically complete the execution. Instead, the designated subsection has been established as the location upon which Orbertall must discharge its terminal result. The Sixth Magician must therefore aim the rifle and strike the precise Immutable Red Spiral for the corresponding portion of universal heat death to be actualized. This requirement gives the weapon an unusually exacting operational character. Its conceptual effect may bypass the personal immortality of the target, but the Sixth Magician’s physical and tactical execution remains significant because the mark must be properly identified, fixed, and struck. A discharge that fails to intersect the designated spiral does not automatically produce the intended terminal result merely because the weapon has been pointed in the target’s general direction. Conversely, once the precise correspondence is struck, the outcome is not determined by whether the projectile possesses enough conventional force to penetrate the target’s body. The discharge activates the previously established cosmological ending, causing the selected universal subsection to reach its terminal condition without requiring the target’s individual physical defenses to be overcome through ordinary damage. In this respect, Orbertall resembles the Mystic Eyes of Death Perception only superficially, as both may involve a visible indication of death and a precise physical action that actualizes the corresponding result. Their underlying principles remain entirely different. The Mystic Eyes perceive an ending belonging to the target, while Orbertall creates a designation through which the greater Universe’s ending can be imposed upon the target’s portion of reality. The same distinction separates the weapon from the Black Barrel, one of the Atlas Institute’s extraordinary conceptual armaments, whose principle involves the imposition of natural lifespan and the measurement of a target’s Life Scale. Black Barrel is particularly effective against extraordinary existences because its governing concept allows it to inflict consequences associated with finite life upon beings that would otherwise resist ordinary destruction. Orbertall does not calculate the target’s natural lifespan, impose mortality upon its body, or increase its destructive effect according to the amount of time the target should possess before dying. The target may genuinely have no personal lifespan to measure. Its immortality may be absolute within the scope of its individual constitution. Nevertheless, the weapon can still operate because the corresponding terminal condition belongs to the Universe rather than the target. This also distinguishes Orbertall from the conceptual imposition of death exercised against beings such as Tiamat, whose extraordinary nature as the Mother of Genesis prevented her from dying under ordinary conditions. King Hassan’s intervention involved granting a Concept of Death to an existence whose fundamental relationship with mortality was otherwise exceptional. Orbertall does not follow that procedure. It does not change the target’s constitution to make death possible. It changes the cosmological condition of the subsection within which that constitution exists. The difference is particularly significant against extraterrestrial Ultimate Ones such as ORT, whose lack of an ordinary Concept of Death and extraordinary capacity for autonomous restoration render conventional methods of killing ineffective. ORT’s biological functions can be restored even after catastrophic damage, and its cells possess an extraordinary independence that makes the destruction of individual organs insufficient to guarantee its elimination. Orbertall does not attempt to defeat this constitution by identifying a vital organ, exhausting its regenerative capacity through repeated attacks, or forcing the creature to acquire terrestrial mortality. If the Sixth Magic successfully designates the universal subsection encompassing ORT’s complete relevant existence, the discharge actualizes the terminal condition of that subsection, removing the cosmological foundation supporting the designated presence rather than merely damaging the biological structures that would otherwise regenerate. This makes the attack dangerous to existences possessing no personal Concept of Death without requiring the Sixth Magician to contradict their inherent immortality. The target has not died because an intrinsic defect was discovered within its existence. It has been eliminated because the greater cosmological subsection containing that existence has already reached its ending. The same reasoning applies to beings whose survival depends upon external sources of energy, environmental continuity, spiritual foundations, or unusual forms of existence, provided their actual existence remains included within the universal framework addressed by the weapon. The important distinction is between the target’s personal continuity and the continuity of the system supporting its presence. A being may possess inexhaustible life within a finite cosmological framework without acquiring the ability to preserve that framework against its own ending. Orbertall exploits this asymmetry, making the immortality of the individual irrelevant to the terminal condition of the greater whole. However, this does not mean that the rifle automatically operates beyond every cosmological boundary or acquires unrestricted authority over the Swirl of the Root. In TYPE-MOON’s metaphysics, the term World frequently designates a particular Texture or conceptual order covering the surface of a planet, while the physical Universe and the metaphysical source of existence are not interchangeable with those planetary layers. The Human Order, the Reverse Side of the World, and the laws governing particular Textures are aspects of reality whose relationships with the greater cosmos must be distinguished from the totality of universal spacetime. Orbertall’s conceptual target is not simply a Texture, nor does its operation depend exclusively upon the mortality of Earth’s Human Order. It addresses the encompassing cosmological framework containing the designated existence, making it fundamentally broader than an attack restricted to a particular planetary layer. An individual existing within the Human Order is therefore not protected merely by possessing an existence incompatible with the ordinary laws of that Texture, because the weapon does not need to rely upon those laws to establish the relevant cosmological subsection. Likewise, the presence of an alien system capable of overwriting local physical laws, such as ORT’s Crystal Valley, does not automatically remove the alien existence from the broader Universe in which the interaction takes place. The weapon’s applicability is determined by cosmological containment rather than conformity to a particular terrestrial law. Nevertheless, a genuinely independent existence whose complete foundation is situated outside the universal framework being targeted would require a corresponding cosmological relationship before Orbertall could designate its ending. This qualification does not diminish the weapon’s stated ability to kill deathless beings contained within the Universe; it identifies the precise metaphysical requirement that makes that ability possible. The Sixth Magician must address an actual universal subsection, not simply declare the death of something unrelated to the cosmic framework being reconstructed. Once the target has been fixed and the Immutable Red Spiral struck, the resulting phenomenon manifests as a localized absence within the continuing Universe. The target does not necessarily explode, burn, decompose, collapse into ordinary particles, or leave behind remains corresponding to its former material structure. Instead, the selected subsection is brought to its terminal condition, producing a small but profound discontinuity in the reality previously occupied by the target. The resulting void must not be confused with ordinary empty space, since a vacuum remains a valid region of spacetime governed by the physical laws of its Universe. Orbertall’s void represents the aftermath of a subsection whose cosmological continuity has been prematurely terminated through Retroupdate. The surrounding region continues to exist, but the designated part has been removed from the ongoing physical and historical canvas. From an ordinary observer’s perspective, the result may resemble the sudden appearance of a small gaping absence where the target had previously stood. From a thaumaturgical perspective, however, the phenomenon is far more disturbing because the missing region is not merely deprived of matter. Its ordinary participation in the Universe’s continued existence has been interrupted. The weapon therefore inflicts two inseparable consequences: the elimination of the target and the removal of the corresponding subsection of the cosmic framework. This distinction explains why Orbertall cannot be accurately classified as an ordinary Anti-Unit weapon despite its ability to designate an individual opponent. Its immediate target may be a single existence, but the mechanism of destruction operates through the ending of a portion of the Universe itself. Nor does the weapon necessarily discharge a conventional Anti-World attack that attempts to annihilate the complete surrounding environment. Instead, it concentrates a cosmological terminal phenomenon upon an infinitesimal designated subsection, producing a level of conceptual effect disproportionate to the apparent scale of the shot. Its destructive significance is not measured by the diameter of the beam, the amount of visible energy released, or the size of the resulting void, but by the nature of the condition imposed. An attack capable of destroying an entire planet through ordinary physical force might leave the planetary region as a collection of matter and radiation, while Orbertall could produce a much smaller apparent wound by terminating the cosmic subsection supporting a single individual. The former possesses tremendous physical scale; the latter represents a violation of the relationship between a constituent existence and the continued actuality of its Universe. This makes the rifle especially dangerous to opponents whose defenses are founded upon the assumption that personal immortality or resistance to physical destruction is sufficient to guarantee survival. An indestructible body cannot prevent the ending of the greater reality containing it merely by remaining indestructible according to its own internal principles. Even an existence that has transcended ordinary biological functions may remain vulnerable if the universal subsection corresponding to its presence can be successfully fixed and terminated. At the same time, Orbertall’s very precision creates an extraordinary danger for its wielder. The Sixth Magician cannot treat the destruction of a universal subsection as an inconsequential process simply because the resulting wound may be physically small. Once the corresponding portion of the Universe’s ending has been actualized, the affected region may no longer possess the ordinary continuity required for conventional restoration. Healing Magecraft, resurrection, reconstruction of material structures, and attempts to reverse physical damage generally presuppose that the underlying reality in which those processes occur remains available. Orbertall directly attacks that underlying reality, and the result may therefore be irreversible through ordinary methods. The absence created by the discharge is not a conventional wound that can be healed by accelerating cellular recovery or replacing destroyed matter. It is a local cosmological ending whose causal prerequisites have been bypassed, meaning there may be no ordinary sequence of physical events that can simply be reversed to restore the lost subsection. Even the restoration of the target’s body from an external record would not necessarily restore the portion of universal continuity that Orbertall removed. A truly extraordinary intervention capable of reconstructing the relevant cosmological framework might theoretically address such damage, but the Sixth Magic does not guarantee that restoration will be possible, and the firing of Orbertall does not automatically provide its creator with a means of undoing the result. This is the weapon’s greatest practical danger. Because the designated subsection includes the cosmological foundation corresponding to the target’s existence, inaccurate targeting or an incomplete understanding of the subject’s relationship with its surroundings may produce unintended consequences. A being whose existence is distributed through multiple vessels, informational structures, or spiritual manifestations may require a designation encompassing more than the immediately visible body. Conversely, a poorly defined target whose existence is intertwined with a broader environmental phenomenon may risk involving surrounding cosmological structures that the Sixth Magician never intended to remove. The weapon’s effectiveness is therefore inseparable from the accuracy with which the intended subsection is identified, and its ability to eliminate extraordinary opponents does not relieve the wielder of the obligation to distinguish the target from the larger reality in which it exists. The Counter Force represents an additional consideration because both Gaia and Alaya function to preserve the continued existence of the planet and humanity, respectively, intervening against threats to their survival through mechanisms that do not necessarily resemble conscious hostility. A weapon capable of removing subsections of the universal framework could constitute a particularly dangerous abnormality if employed in a manner threatening the continuity of the World or the Human Order. The Counter Force might consequently respond to the circumstances surrounding Orbertall’s use, attempting to prevent a catastrophic discharge or eliminate the conditions leading to widespread cosmological damage. However, such intervention would not automatically establish that the Counter Force could reverse a completed act of universal subsection termination, nor would it necessarily possess immediate authority over the fourteenth-dimensional Replica Universe from which the weapon’s reconstructive principle originates. Its response would depend upon the scale and nature of the threat presented to the protected World. For the Sixth Magician, this introduces a peculiar contradiction: he possesses a separate Universe whose continued existence supports his own extraordinary durability, yet the weapon he has created can permanently injure portions of the Actual Universe upon which ordinary beings depend. His own cosmological foundation may remain intact even when the surrounding reality suffers an irreversible wound, making the consequences of his attack potentially more significant for the World than for the Magician himself. Orbertall is consequently an instrument requiring exceptional restraint, not because its conceptual principle is uncertain, but because its successful activation produces a result more final than ordinary destruction. The weapon does not rely upon an opponent’s fear of death, nor does it need that opponent to recognize or comprehend the terminal condition being imposed. Once the Immutable Red Spiral has been established and correctly struck, the corresponding universal subsection is made to inherit an ending that belongs to the greater cosmological whole, irrespective of whether the individual existence contained within that subsection would otherwise have continued indefinitely. This is the essence of the designation All-Hanging Heat Death. The ending hangs over all things contained within the Universe, not because every constituent possesses an identical personal lifespan, but because their existence remains included within a greater framework whose ultimate fate is independent of their individual ability to survive. An immortal existence can remain immortal within its own constitution, an informational entity can remain without an ordinary physical body, and an Ultimate One can remain foreign to Earth’s natural Concept of Death. None of these conditions automatically establishes independence from the cosmological framework containing that existence. Orbertall does not need to disprove those extraordinary properties. It identifies the much greater ending within which their continuing existence occupies only an infinitesimal part. The final operation is therefore neither the creation of a personal death nor the conventional destruction of an indestructible body, but the premature actualization of the Universe’s terminal condition upon the subsection corresponding to that body. The Sixth Magician must identify that subsection, manifest the Immutable Red Spiral, and strike the exact designation with Orbertall. When the operation succeeds, the designated portion of the Universe reaches its ending, the target ceases to remain within the continuing cosmos, and a small void appears where its existence and the corresponding fragment of universal reality once resided. The rest of the Universe remains unaffected by the passage of its own distant terminal age, continuing to evolve toward a future that the selected subsection has already experienced. Thus, the rifle does not end the Universe in order to kill an individual. It ends only the infinitesimal portion of the Universe in which that individual exists, making the greater cosmological finality precede the individual ending that may never have existed in the first place. All-Hanging Heat Death — Orbertall is therefore a conceptual armament that embodies a principle more profound than the negation of immortality: the deathlessness of an individual cannot guarantee the deathlessness of the Universe containing that individual, and the Sixth Magic can actualize the latter without ever invoking the former.


